ge_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#app","content":"`GET /app/update` returns `status`, `current`, `latest` (the newest final release on PyPI, once known) and `checked_at` (Unix seconds of the last successful check). `status` is `checking` (the first check has not finished), `available`, `current`, `failed` (no check has succeeded yet; later failures keep the last good answer) or `disabled` (`server.check_updates` is off).","locale":"en"},"8764":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-110","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#settings","content":"`GET /settings` returns the current settings: `data_dir`, `config_path`, `server` (host, port, `strict_port`, `access_token_configured`, `model_api_key_configured`, allowed CIDRs/hosts/origins, `max_body_bytes`, `max_account_retries`, `default_model`, `auto_refresh`, `auto_checkin`, `check_updates`, `stats_keep_days`), `providers` (each provider's `id`, `enabled`, account count, the names of its options, its network settings), `network`, `playground`, and:","locale":"en"},"8765":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-111","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#settings","content":"`restart_required`: a saved `server.host` / `server.port` differs from what this process started with and needs a restart.","locale":"en"},"8766":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-112","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#settings","content":"`playground.workspace_path`, `playground.shell_in_effect` and `playground.shells` (read-only): where the tools work, the shell commands run in when a call names none (`auto` resolved), and the shells installed on this machine.","locale":"en"},"8767":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-113","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#settings","content":"`listening`: the socket actually in use; `port` is the bound port, `requested_port` the one the search started from, and `fallback` means the requested port was taken and another was used (never a reason to restart).","locale":"en"},"8768":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-114","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#settings","content":"The keys themselves are never returned.","locale":"en"},"8769":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-115","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#settings","content":"`PATCH /settings` takes partial settings in the shape of `config.json`, deep-merges them, validates the result, saves it to the config file and applies it to the running gateway, then returns the new settings:","locale":"en"},"8770":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-116","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#settings","content":"Setting `server.access_token` or `server.model_api_key` to `null` (or an empty string) clears it.","locale":"en"},"8771":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-117","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#settings","content":"Invalid values answer `400` with the reason, for example binding a non-loopback address without both `security.allow_cidrs` and `server.access_token`.","locale":"en"},"8772":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-118","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#settings","content":"Changing the listening host or port turns `restart_required` to `true`.","locale":"en"},"8773":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-119","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#settings","content":"`{\"playground\": {\"approval\": \"auto\"}}` is saved as `workspace`, the mode's new name.","locale":"en"},"8774":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-120","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#settings","content":"What each setting means is in Configuration file.","locale":"en"},"8775":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-121","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#providers-and-accounts","content":"Each item of `GET /providers` has `id`, `display_name`, `accounts` (anonymous accounts not counted), `account_ids`, `models` (the cached model count; this never asks the upstream), `enabled`, `keyless` (usable without an account) and `requires_authorization` (needs a sign-in or a key). Configured but disabled providers, and providers that could be signed into or given a key but are not configured yet, are listed too.","locale":"en"},"8776":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-122","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#providers-and-accounts","content":"`GET /provider-forms` lists, per provider, the ways to add an account (`method`) with their fields (`key`, `kind`, `required`, `choices`) and defaults.","locale":"en"},"8777":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-123","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#providers-and-accounts","content":"`POST /providers/{provider_id}/accounts` appends one account; the `account` in the body is exactly what you would write in `config.json`:","locale":"en"},"8778":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-124","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#providers-and-accounts","content":"Accounts are appended, never replaced. The provider checks the account first and answers `400` when it is unusable.","locale":"en"},"8779":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-125","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#providers-and-accounts","content":"Without an `id`, one of the form `<provider>-<n>` is generated; an existing `id` answers `409`; an unknown provider answers `404`.","locale":"en"},"8780":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-126","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#providers-and-accounts","content":"A disabled provider is switched back on. The account goes into both the config file and the running pool.","locale":"en"},"8781":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-127","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#providers-and-accounts","content":"`DELETE /providers/{provider_id}/accounts/{account_id}` removes the account from the config file and the running pool and returns `{\"provider\", \"account\", \"removed_from_config\"}`. An account imported from an older data folder, which is not in `config.json`, is removed from the pool only, with `removed_from_config` set to `false`. If neither has it, the answer is `404`.","locale":"en"},"8782":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-128","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#providers-and-accounts","content":"`GET /stations` lists the stations an `agg` account can name with `preset`: `id`, `display_name`, `base_url`, `key_env` (only a hint about which key to have ready; Hoshimi does not read that variable) and `catalog_keyless`. See The agg aggregator.","locale":"en"},"8783":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-129","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#providers-and-accounts","content":"`GET /channels` returns all the local state the Channels page needs in one read, without asking any upstream (balances need upstream requests, so they live in `/credits`):","locale":"en"},"8784":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-130","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#providers-and-accounts","content":"Per provider: `id`, `display_name`, `enabled`, `keyless`, `configured`, `loginable`, `addable`, `forms`, `models`, `options`, `network`, `diagnostics`, `quota` (passive quota), `accounts`, `usage_today`, `recent_checkins` (the last five check-in outcomes) and `status`.","locale":"en"},"8785":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-131","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#providers-and-accounts","content":"`status`: `ok`; `attention` (still serving, but something needs a human: a sign-in, an expired token, a cooled account, rate limiting, or quota at or below 10%); `disabled` (switched off); `empty` (nothing to serve from).","locale":"en"},"8786":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-132","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#providers-and-accounts","content":"Per account: `needs_login`, `refreshable`, `expires_at` (epoch milliseconds), `failures`, `last_error`, `last_ok`, `cooled_reason`, `cooled_seconds`, `usage_today`, `last_used_at`.","locale":"en"},"8787":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-133","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#providers-and-accounts","content":"At the top level: `checkin` (the daily check-in state), `auto_refresh`, `auto_checkin`.","locale":"en"},"8788":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-134","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#providers-and-accounts","content":"`GET /network/diagnostics` returns the latest observation of each kind of network operation per provider: `provider`, `operation`, `kind` (such as `timeout`, `proxy_error`, `connection_error`, `rate_limited`), `status`, `at`, `host`, `route`. Network settings are covered in Network and proxies.","locale":"en"},"8789":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-135","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#model-catalogue","content":"`GET /models` returns `levels` (the three output budgets `light`, `balanced`, `deep`) and `data`. Each item of `data`:","locale":"en"},"8790":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-136","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#model-catalogue","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"8791":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-137","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#model-catalogue","content":"Notes","locale":"en"},"8792":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-138","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#model-catalogue","content":"`id`, `provider`, `name`","locale":"en"},"8793":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-139","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#model-catalogue","content":"Model id, provider, display name","locale":"en"},"8794":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-140","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#model-catalogue","content":"`wire`","locale":"en"},"8795":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-141","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#model-catalogue","content":"The upstream protocol: `chat`, `responses`, `messages` and so on","locale":"en"},"8796":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-142","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#model-catalogue","content":"`vision`, `reasoning`, `tools`","locale":"en"},"8797":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-143","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#model-catalogue","content":"Reads images, reasons, calls tools (`tools` is `null` when unknown)","locale":"en"},"8798":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-144","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#model-catalogue","content":"`context_window`, `max_output`","locale":"en"},"8799":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-145","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#model-catalogue","content":"Context length and maximum output (`0` when unknown)","locale":"en"},"8800":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-146","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#model-catalogue","content":"`can_disable_thinking`","locale":"en"},"8801":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-147","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#model-catalogue","content":"Whether thinking can be turned off","locale":"en"},"8802":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-148","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#model-catalogue","content":"`region_sensitive`","locale":"en"},"8803":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-149","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#model-catalogue","content":"Whether availability depends on region","locale":"en"},"8804":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-150","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#model-catalogue","content":"`free`","locale":"en"},"8805":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-151","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#model-catalogue","content":"Whether the station says it is free; `null` when it says nothing","locale":"en"},"8806":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-152","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#model-catalogue","content":"`efforts`, `effort_default`","locale":"en"},"8807":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-153","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#model-catalogue","content":"Effort options (`id`, `name`, `description`, `is_default`, `tokens`) and the default level","locale":"en"},"8808":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-154","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#model-catalogue","content":"`probe`","locale":"en"},"8809":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-155","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#model-catalogue","content":"The latest availability verdict, or `null` if never probed","locale":"en"},"8810":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-156","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#model-catalogue","content":"`unavailable`","locale":"en"},"8811":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-157","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#model-catalogue","content":"Whether the model is held out (the station answered 404/410 on every account)","locale":"en"},"8812":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-158","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#model-catalogue","content":"`GET /catalog/stream` is SSE: first a `snapshot` event listing each provider's cached models (status `loading`); then a `provider` event as each provider finishes refreshing (status `ready`, `failed`, or `timeout` after 20 seconds, with `error`, `last_success`, `retry_at` and `source`); finally `done`. While waiting it sends `: keep-alive` comments.","locale":"en"},"8813":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-159","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#model-catalogue","content":"`POST /models/unavailable/reset` lets every held-out model back in and returns `{\"cleared\": <count>}`.","locale":"en"},"8814":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-160","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#availability-probes","content":"`GET /probe` returns `running`, `at` (when the last round finished) and `results` (model → `state`, `detail`, `latency_ms`, `ttft_ms`, `at`). `state` is `available`, `region-blocked`, `unavailable`, `throttled` or `unknown`.","locale":"en"},"8815":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-161","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#availability-probes","content":"`POST /probe` starts a round in the background; the body is optional:","locale":"en"},"8816":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-162","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#availability-probes","content":"Without `models`, or with an empty list, every model of the providers that need probing is probed. The answer is the same snapshot plus `started` (whether a new round actually began; `false` while one is already running, as rounds do not stack) and `unresolved` (model names that could not be resolved). What probes mean is in Model and account behaviour.","locale":"en"},"8817":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-163","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#credential-renewal","content":"`GET /refresh` returns `auto_refresh` and, per account, `provider`, `account`, `refreshable`, `needs_login`, `expires_at`, `failures`, `last_error`, `last_ok`.","locale":"en"},"8818":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-164","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#credential-renewal","content":"`POST /refresh` renews credentials that are due, with an optional body `{\"provider\": \"<provider>\", \"force\": true}` (`force` renews every refreshable account, due or not). It returns one outcome per account: `ok`, `persisted` (the new credential was saved to the config), `terminal` (the station refused the refresh token; the account needs a new sign-in) and `error`.","locale":"en"},"8819":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-165","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#balances-and-check-in","content":"Endpoint","locale":"en"},"8820":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-166","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#balances-and-check-in","content":"Parameters","locale":"en"},"8821":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-167","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#balances-and-check-in","content":"Returns","locale":"en"},"8822":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-168","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#balances-and-check-in","content":"`GET /credits`","locale":"en"},"8823":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-169","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#balances-and-check-in","content":"`provider` (optional)","locale":"en"},"8824":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-170","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#balances-and-check-in","content":"`rows` (each account's `available`, `unit`, `message`; asks the upstream), `passive` (remaining quota read off ordinary response headers, marked `stale` after five minutes), `cooled` (accounts out of rotation, with reason `rate_limited` or `policy_blocked` and seconds left), `checkin`","locale":"en"},"8825":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-171","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#balances-and-check-in","content":"`GET /credits/checkins`","locale":"en"},"8826":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-172","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#balances-and-check-in","content":"`provider` (optional), `limit` (1–500, default 50)","locale":"en"},"8827":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-173","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#balances-and-check-in","content":"Check-in history, newest first, daily rounds and on-demand claims alike; kept 365 days","locale":"en"},"8828":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-174","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#balances-and-check-in","content":"`POST /credits/claim`","locale":"en"},"8829":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-175","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#balances-and-check-in","content":"Body `{\"provider\": \"<provider>\"}`; omitted means every provider","locale":"en"},"8830":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-176","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#balances-and-check-in","content":"Each account's `status`, `credits`, `covers_today`, `message`; a station already claimed today answers `already`","locale":"en"},"8831":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-177","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#sign-in","content":"Browser authorisation and device-code sign-ins take a few steps:","locale":"en"},"8832":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-178","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#start","content":"This returns a session: `id`, `provider`, `status`, `login_url` (once the station issues one), `user_code` and `instructions` (for device codes), `expires_at`, `waiting_for` and `message`. `GET /login/providers` lists the providers you can sign into.","locale":"en"},"8833":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-179","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#poll","content":"Open `login_url` in a browser and finish there, then poll until `status` moves from `pending` to `succeeded` (`account_id` is the new account) or `failed` (`message` says why). An unknown session answers `404`.","locale":"en"},"8834":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-180","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#send-input-or-cancel","content":"When the station needs more input (`waiting_for` is not empty), send `{\"session_id\": \"…\", \"value\": \"…\"}` to `POST /login/input`. `POST /login/cancel?session_id=<session-id>` cancels a sign-in in progress.","locale":"en"},"8835":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-181","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#send-input-or-cancel","content":"How each station signs in is covered in Channels.","locale":"en"},"8836":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-182","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"Parameters of `GET /stats`:","locale":"en"},"8837":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-183","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"Parameter","locale":"en"},"8838":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-184","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"Notes","locale":"en"},"8839":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-185","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"`range`","locale":"en"},"8840":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-186","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"`24h`, `day`, `7d` (default), `30d`, `90d`","locale":"en"},"8841":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-187","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"`date`","locale":"en"},"8842":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-188","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"The date for `range=day`, `YYYY-MM-DD` in server local time (today by default); a future or malformed date answers `400`","locale":"en"},"8843":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-189","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"It returns `totals`, `previous` (the equal span just before; for `day` the day before, and for today only up to the same time of day), `latency` (average, median and P95 of time to first token and generation speed), a zero-filled `series`, breakdowns by model, provider, account and origin, `lifetime`, and `since`, `until` (exclusive), `date`, `granularity`, `hourly` and `server_time`. `24h` and `day` are hourly (23 or 25 hours on a daylight-saving change), the rest daily. Hourly data is kept 120 days and daily data forever; a day without hourly data has `hourly` set to `false`.","locale":"en"},"8844":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-190","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"`GET /stats/days` returns every local date with usage (`date`, `calls`, `tokens`, `failed`), oldest first, plus `first` and `today`, for a calendar.","locale":"en"},"8845":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-191","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"`GET /stats/calls` returns individual calls, newest first, over the whole retention period (`server.stats_keep_days`, 90 days by default):","locale":"en"},"8846":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-192","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"Parameter","locale":"en"},"8847":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-193","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"Notes","locale":"en"},"8848":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-194","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"`limit`","locale":"en"},"8849":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-195","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"1–200, default 50","locale":"en"},"8850":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-196","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"`before`","locale":"en"},"8851":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-197","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"Paging cursor: the `next` of the previous page","locale":"en"},"8852":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-198","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"`model`, `provider`, `origin`, `ok`","locale":"en"},"8853":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-199","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"Exact filters; `origin` is `chat`, `responses`, `messages`, `classify`, `playground` and so on","locale":"en"},"8854":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-200","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"`account`","locale":"en"},"8855":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-201","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"An account id, or `provider/account`","locale":"en"},"8856":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-202","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"`since`, `until`","locale":"en"},"8857":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-203","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"ISO 8601 times (with an offset; without one, server local time); `until` is exclusive","locale":"en"},"8858":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-204","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"`q`","locale":"en"},"8859":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-205","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"Case-insensitive search in the model, provider, account, error code, error message and finish reason","locale":"en"},"8860":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-206","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"Each record has `seq`, `at`, `model`, `provider`, `account`, `origin`, `effort`, `stream`, `ok`, the token counts, `ttft_ms`, `tps`, `elapsed_ms`, `attempts`, `finish_reason`, `error_code`, `error_message` and more.","locale":"en"},"8861":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-207","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"`DELETE /stats` clears every counter and recorded call and returns `{\"cleared_at\": …}`; calls in flight are still recorded when they finish.","locale":"en"},"8862":{"id":"/en/docs/api-management-208","page_id":"/en/docs/api-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-management#usage-statistics","content":"`GET /stats/live` is SSE with `data: <json>` frames: first a `snapshot` (calls in flight, today's totals, the latest calls), then `started`, `progress` and `finished` events, with a `ping` every 15 seconds. A reader that falls too far behind is disconnected; reconnecting brings a fresh snapshot. Token counts of calls in flight are estimated from characters. How usage is recorded is in Usage statistics.","locale":"en"},"8863":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","type":"page","content":"OpenAI-compatible API","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","API reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api-openai","locale":"en"},"8864":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-0","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai","content":"Reference for the OpenAI-compatible endpoints under /v1: request fields, responses and stream events of Chat Completions and Responses, the model list, model routing, how reasoning effort is mapped, and classification.","locale":"en"},"8865":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-1","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs