 fields share their definitions and conversion logic with `GET /api/v1/models` and `GET /api/v1/catalog/stream` (Management API). These extend the OpenAI response format. When model metadata is unavailable, defaults apply: `vision` and `reasoning` are `false`, `context_window` is `131072`, and `max_output` is `32768`; defaults are not upstream-confirmed capabilities. Requests with `limit` may initially return these defaults, then return known metadata once catalogue discovery completes.","locale":"en"},"9007":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-143","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-routing","content":"The `model` of a request is resolved like this:","locale":"en"},"9008":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-144","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-routing","content":"`provider/model`, where `provider` is an enabled provider id: that provider serves it, and everything after the first slash (further slashes included) is the upstream model name.","locale":"en"},"9009":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-145","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-routing","content":"Otherwise the first provider, in provider order, whose catalogue has the name.","locale":"en"},"9010":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-146","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-routing","content":"If none has it and only one provider is enabled, the name goes to that provider as is.","locale":"en"},"9011":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-147","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-routing","content":"Otherwise `404`, code `model_not_found`.","locale":"en"},"9012":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-148","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-routing","content":"When `model` is absent, `server.default_model` is used (**Settings** › **General** › **Default model**, or `hoshimi serve --default-model`).","locale":"en"},"9013":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-149","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#model-routing","content":"Once a provider is chosen, Hoshimi rotates and retries across its accounts. When the station answers 404/410 for a model on every account, the model is held out for a while (`503`, `model_unavailable`). See Model and account behaviour.","locale":"en"},"9014":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-150","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`reasoning_effort` (Chat) and `reasoning.effort` (Responses) follow these rules. A request without an effort level is not touched, and a caller's own `max_tokens` stays as it is.","locale":"en"},"9015":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-151","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"**Models with their own thinking menu** (the **Models** page shows several levels, for example `disabled` / `low` / `high` / `max`): a level on the menu is used as is; anything else goes through these aliases:","locale":"en"},"9016":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-152","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"Request","locale":"en"},"9017":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-153","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"Becomes","locale":"en"},"9018":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-154","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`minimal`, `light`","locale":"en"},"9019":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-155","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`low`","locale":"en"},"9020":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-156","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`balanced`","locale":"en"},"9021":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-157","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`medium`","locale":"en"},"9022":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-158","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`deep`","locale":"en"},"9023":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-159","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`high`","locale":"en"},"9024":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-160","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`xhigh`","locale":"en"},"9025":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-161","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`max`","locale":"en"},"9026":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-162","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"If the result is still not on the menu, the model's default level is used. The chosen level is written into the upstream request the way the model declares; the output ceiling is then the smaller of the model's capacity and the request's own value, whatever the level.","locale":"en"},"9027":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-163","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"**Other reasoning models** use Hoshimi's three output budgets (one ceiling shared by thinking and the answer):","locale":"en"},"9028":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-164","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"Level","locale":"en"},"9029":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-165","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"Written in the request as","locale":"en"},"9030":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-166","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"Output ceiling","locale":"en"},"9031":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-167","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`light`","locale":"en"},"9032":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-168","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`light`, `minimal`, `low`","locale":"en"},"9033":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-169","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"2048","locale":"en"},"9034":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-170","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`balanced` (default)","locale":"en"},"9035":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-171","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`balanced`, `medium`, and anything unrecognised","locale":"en"},"9036":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-172","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"8192","locale":"en"},"9037":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-173","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`deep`","locale":"en"},"9038":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-174","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"`deep`, `high`, `xhigh`, `max`","locale":"en"},"9039":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-175","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"The model's maximum output","locale":"en"},"9040":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-176","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"For a model whose thinking cannot be turned off, each ceiling is doubled.","locale":"en"},"9041":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-177","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"The ceiling never exceeds the model's maximum output or the request's own `max_tokens`, and never drops below 512.","locale":"en"},"9042":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-178","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"For these models the `reasoning_effort` / `reasoning` fields are not sent upstream; only `max_tokens` controls the budget.","locale":"en"},"9043":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-179","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#reasoning-effort","content":"For a model that neither reasons nor has a thinking menu, Hoshimi leaves the effort fields alone and passes them to the upstream as they are. Each model's levels and default are on the **Models** page, or in `efforts` and `effort_default` of `GET /api/v1/models`.","locale":"en"},"9044":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-180","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#classification","content":"TypeSafe classifiers are not chat models. They are not in `/v1/models` and are used through their own endpoints (with an account on the `typesafe` provider).","locale":"en"},"9045":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-181","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#classification","content":"The body sent to `POST /v1/classify`:","locale":"en"},"9046":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-182","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#classification","content":"`model` must be an id from `/v1/classifiers`; otherwise the answer is `404` (`Select a classifier from /v1/classifiers.`).","locale":"en"},"9047":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-183","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#classification","content":"`state` is an object and `questions` a non-empty object; each question's `type` is `bool`, `score` or `choice`, and its other fields go to the upstream unchanged. Images are not supported.","locale":"en"},"9048":{"id":"/en/docs/api-openai-184","page_id":"/en/docs/api-openai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-openai#classification","content":"The response is `{\"provider\", \"model\", \"answers\", \"usage\"}`: a `bool` answer is `{\"type\": \"bool\", \"probability\": …}`; a `score` answer carries `score` and `confidence`; a `choice` answer carries `choice`, `probabilities` and `confidence`.","locale":"en"},"9049":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","type":"page","content":"Playground API","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","API reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api-playground","locale":"en"},"9050":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-0","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/api-playground","content":"Reference for the /api/v1/playground routes: conversations as message trees, sending and retrying with streamed Server-Sent Events, tool steps, approvals, steering, background commands, attachments, titles, branches and sessions.","locale":"en"},"9051":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-1","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api-playground#routes","content":"Routes","locale":"en"},"9052":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-2","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api-playground#conversations","content":"Conversations","locale":"en"},"9053":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-3","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/api-playground#the-conversation-object","content":"The conversation object","locale":"en"},"9054":{"id":"/en/docs/api-playground-4","page_id":"/en/docs/api-playground","ty