":"`--refresh / --no-refresh`","locale":"en"},"9701":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-52","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"`--refresh`","locale":"en"},"9702":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-53","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"Renew credentials on a timer (off: rotate tokens by hand)","locale":"en"},"9703":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-54","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"`--checkin / --no-checkin`","locale":"en"},"9704":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-55","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"`--checkin`","locale":"en"},"9705":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-56","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"Daily check-in timer for free credits (off: claim by hand)","locale":"en"},"9706":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-57","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"`--ui / --no-ui`","locale":"en"},"9707":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-58","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"`--ui`","locale":"en"},"9708":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-59","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"Serve the Web UI next to the API; `--no-ui` serves the API only","locale":"en"},"9709":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-60","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"These options apply to this start only and are not written to `config.json`. An empty string for `--access-token`, `--model-api-key` or `--default-model` has no effect; the configured value is kept.","locale":"en"},"9710":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-61","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"`serve` always sets credential renewal and daily check-in from these two switches, and both default to on. So even with `server.auto_refresh: false` or `server.auto_checkin: false` in `config.json` (or after turning them off under **Settings › Automation**), they are on again after a start with plain `hoshimi serve`. To keep them off at start, add `--no-refresh` or `--no-checkin`.","locale":"en"},"9711":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-62","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"What happens at start:","locale":"en"},"9712":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-63","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"The configuration is read, the options above are applied on top, and the channels are built from it.","locale":"en"},"9713":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-64","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"If the address is not a loopback address (`127.*`, `localhost`, `::1`), a warning is printed. Without a tool access key the server refuses to start (exit code 4); without a model API key it warns that external model APIs accept requests without a key. `security.allow_cidrs` must also be configured, or the server refuses to start (exit code 4). See Security.","locale":"en"},"9714":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-65","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"The port is bound. If it is taken, the next port is tried, up to 65535, then wrapping around from 1024; a move is logged as `Port 10600 is unavailable. Using port 10601.` With `--strict-port` only the one port is tried. If no port can be bound, the command ends with exit code 3.","locale":"en"},"9715":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-66","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"The address is written to `server.json` in the data folder, the line `SERVER_READY url=<address>` is printed on standard output, and `Hoshimi running on <address>` is logged. When listening on `0.0.0.0` or `::`, the printed address uses `127.0.0.1`.","locale":"en"},"9716":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-67","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"With `--open`, the address is opened in a browser a moment later.","locale":"en"},"9717":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-68","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#serve","content":"Press Ctrl+C to stop; `server.json` is removed on exit. Without a built Web UI (a source install that was not built), the server logs a warning and serves the API only.","locale":"en"},"9718":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-69","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"Validate the configuration and report which channels and accounts would be served, without starting the server.","locale":"en"},"9719":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-70","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"Option","locale":"en"},"9720":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-71","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"9721":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-72","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"`--json`","locale":"en"},"9722":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-73","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"Print JSON","locale":"en"},"9723":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-74","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"It applies the same checks as saving settings in the Web UI: the network policy and proxy URLs, the port range, the limits, the Playground settings, and the security rules (for example, listening on a non-local address needs both `security.allow_cidrs` and `server.access_token`; `security.allow_origins` needs `server.access_token`). A problem ends the command with exit code 2 and the reason.","locale":"en"},"9724":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-75","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"Each channel is written `<id>:<accounts>`; a channel that needs no account is marked `(keyless)` while it has none. With no channel enabled at all, it prints an error line and exits with code 2.","locale":"en"},"9725":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-76","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"The `--json` fields:","locale":"en"},"9726":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-77","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"9727":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-78","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"Content","locale":"en"},"9728":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-79","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"`config_path`","locale":"en"},"9729":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-80","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"Path of the configuration file","locale":"en"},"9730":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-81","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"`providers`","locale":"en"},"9731":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-82","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"`{channel id: account count}`","locale":"en"},"9732":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-83","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"`accounts`","locale":"en"},"9733":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-84","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"Total number of accounts","locale":"en"},"9734":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-85","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"`keyless`","locale":"en"},"9735":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-86","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"Ids of the channels that need no account","locale":"en"},"9736":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-87","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"`models`","locale":"en"},"9737":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-88","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"Number of models","locale":"en"},"9738":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-89","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#check","content":"With `--json`, the exit code is 0 even when no channel is enabled.","locale":"en"},"9739":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-90","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#models","content":"List the available models: the same list `GET /v1/models` returns.","locale":"en"},"9740":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-91","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#models","content":"Option","locale":"en"},"9741":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-92","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#models","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"9742":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-93","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#models","content":"`--provider TEXT`","locale":"en"},"9743":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-94","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#models","content":"Only show this channel's models (a channel id, such as `kilo`)","locale":"en"},"9744":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-95","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#models","content":"`--json`","locale":"en"},"9745":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-96","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#models","content":"Print JSON: `[{\"id\": \"<model id>\", \"provider\": \"<channel id>\"}, …]`","locale":"en"},"9746":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-97","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#models","content":"The table has **Model** and **Provider** columns. A model id offered by several channels is listed once, under the channel that comes first.","locale":"en"},"9747":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-98","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#providers","content":"List the configured channels with their account and model counts.","locale":"en"},"9748":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-99","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#providers","content":"Option","locale":"en"},"9749":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-100","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#providers","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"9750":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-101","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#providers","content":"`--json`","locale":"en"},"9751":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-102","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#providers","content":"Print JSON","locale":"en"},"9752":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-103","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#providers","content":"The table's columns are **Id**, **Name**, **Accounts** and **Models**; switched-off channels are listed under it as `disabled: …`. The account count leaves out the built-in anonymous identity of the anonymous channels.","locale":"en"},"9753":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-104","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#providers","content":"The `--json` shape:","locale":"en"},"9754":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-105","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#providers","content":"`accounts` lists account ids, `disabled` the ids of switched-off channels. Model counts depend on the upstream catalogue at the time.","locale":"en"},"9755":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-106","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#stations","content":"List the stations an `agg` account can name as its `preset`.","locale":"en"},"9756":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-107","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#stations","content":"Option","locale":"en"},"9757":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-108","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#stations","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"9758":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-109","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#stations","content":"`--json`","locale":"en"},"9759":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-110","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#stations","content":"Print JSON","locale":"en"},"9760":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-111","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#stations","content":"The table's columns are **Id**, **Name**, **Base URL** and **Key env**, followed by a usage hint:","locale":"en"},"9761":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-112","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#stations","content":"**Key env** is only the environment variable name the upstream's own tools use, so you know which key to look for; Hoshimi does not read these variables, and the key goes into the account in `config.json`. `--json` prints `{\"stations\": [...]}`, each entry with `id`, `display_name`, `base_url`, `key_env` and `catalog_keyless` (whether the model list can be fetched without a key). Usage and every preset are in agg aggregators.","locale":"en"},"9762":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-113","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#version","content":"Show the versions of Hoshimi, Python and the main components (fastapi, uvicorn, pydantic, typer, httpx, rich).","locale":"en"},"9763":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-114","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#version","content":"Option","locale":"en"},"9764":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-115","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#version","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"9765":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-116","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#version","content":"`--json`","locale":"en"},"9766":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-117","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#version","content":"Print JSON: `{\"hoshimi\": \"…\", \"python\": \"…\", \"components\": {\"fastapi\": \"…\", …}}`","locale":"en"},"9767":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-118","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#version","content":"A component that is not installed shows `not installed` in the table and `null` in JSON.","locale":"en"},"9768":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-119","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#env","content":"List the environment variables Hoshimi reads, and those currently set.","locale":"en"},"9769":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-120","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#env","content":"Option","locale":"en"},"9770":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-121","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#env","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"9771":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-122","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#env","content":"`--json`","locale":"en"},"9772":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-123","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#env","content":"Print JSON: `{\"known\": {name: meaning}, \"set\": {name: value}}`","locale":"en"},"9773":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-124","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#env","content":"The first table, **Environment variables**, lists the known variables and what they mean. When any variable starting with `HOSHIMI_` is set in the current environment, a second table, **Set now**, shows their values, with `***` for names containing `TOKEN` or `KEY`. What each variable does is in Environment variables.","locale":"en"},"9774":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-125","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#login","content":"Sign into a station (by browser authorization); when the station hands back the credential, the account is written to `config.json`.","locale":"en"},"9775":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-126","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#login","content":"Argument / option","locale":"en"},"9776":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-127","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#login","content":"Default","locale":"en"},"9777":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-128","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#login","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"9778":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-129","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#login","content":"`[PROVIDER]`","locale":"en"},"9779":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-130","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#login","content":"—","locale":"en"},"9780":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-131","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#login","content":"The station to sign into; omit it to list the stations that offer an interactive login","locale":"en"},"9781":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-132","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#login","content":"`--open / --no-open`","locale":"en"},"9782":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-133","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#login","content":"`--open`","locale":"en"},"9783":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-134","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#login","content":"Open the station's login page in a browser","locale":"en"},"9784":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-135","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#login","content":"`--manual`","locale":"en"},"9785":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-136","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#login","content":"off","locale":"en"},"9786":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-137","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#login","content":"Prompt for the authorization code or callback URL (the input is not echoed)","locale":"en"},"9787":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-138","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#login","content":"Stations with an interactive login: `anthropic`, `buddy`, `cline`, `codearts`, `codex`, `eac`, `gemini`, `github-copilot`, `kilo`, `kimi-coding`, `lobsterai`, `loomy`, `meta`, `minimax`, `openai`, `openrouter`, `qoder`, `qodercn`, `qodercli`, `qodercli-cn`, `raccoon`, `radius`, `trae`, `workbuddy`, `xai`, `zcode`.","locale":"en"},"9788":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-139","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#login","content":"The flow:","locale":"en"},"9789":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-140","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#login","content":"The command asks the station for a login link and prints `Authorize at <link>`; device-code stations also print `Authorization code: <code> — <link>`, the code to enter on the authorization page.","locale":"en"},"9790":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-141","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#login","content":"With `--open`, the link opens in a browser; if no browser can be opened, you are asked to visit it by hand.","locale":"en"},"9791":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-142","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#login","content":"It checks for the result every 2 seconds. On success it prints `Signed into <station> as <account id>.` and the account is in the configuration; on failure it exits with code 1.","locale":"en"},"9792":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-143","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#login","content":"If the station has not answered within 10 minutes, it times out (exit code 1).","locale":"en"},"9793":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-144","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#login","content":"Signing in again with the same station identity replaces that account instead of adding a second one. A station name that is not on the list gives exit code 2.","locale":"en"},"9794":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-145","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#login","content":"`--manual` is for a browser that runs on a different machine from Hoshimi: many stations send the result to a loopback port on this machine, which a browser elsewhere cannot reach. Paste the callback URL the browser finally lands on (or the code the page shows) at the prompt. Each station's login method and callback port are in Free stations.","locale":"en"},"9795":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-146","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#login","content":"A running server does not pick up accounts added by a command-line login until it restarts; signing in on the Web UI's **Channels** page applies at once.","locale":"en"},"9796":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-147","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#configuration","content":"The `config` commands read and write `config.json` in the data folder. Keys are dotted, such as `server.port`, `security.allow_cidrs` or `providers.kilo.enabled`. Every key is listed in Configuration.","locale":"en"},"9797":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-148","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-path","content":"Print the path of the configuration file. It prints where the file will be created even before it exists.","locale":"en"},"9798":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-149","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-show","content":"Show the configuration: the file's contents when it exists, the defaults when it does not. Credentials are shown as `***`.","locale":"en"},"9799":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-150","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-show","content":"Option","locale":"en"},"9800":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-151","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-show","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"9801":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-152","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-show","content":"`--json`","locale":"en"},"9802":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-153","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-show","content":"Print plain JSON (no colour, and no file path on the last line)","locale":"en"},"9803":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-154","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-show","content":"Without `--json`, the JSON is coloured and the last line is the configuration file's path.","locale":"en"},"9804":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-155","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-get","content":"Print one setting as JSON. Credentials are shown as `***`.","locale":"en"},"9805":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-156","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-get","content":"Argument","locale":"en"},"9806":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-157","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-get","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"9807":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-158","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-get","content":"`<KEY>`","locale":"en"},"9808":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-159","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-get","content":"A dotted key, such as `server.port`","locale":"en"},"9809":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-160","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-get","content":"A key that does not exist gives `Unknown setting: <KEY>` and exit code 4. A whole section can be read too:","locale":"en"},"9810":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-161","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-get","content":"Without a configuration file, the readable keys are those the defaults have (the entries under `network`, `server` and `security`).","locale":"en"},"9811":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-162","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-set","content":"Change one setting and save it.","locale":"en"},"9812":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-163","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-set","content":"Argument","locale":"en"},"9813":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-164","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-set","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"9814":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-165","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-set","content":"`<KEY>`","locale":"en"},"9815":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-166","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-set","content":"A dotted key, such as `server.port` or `security.allow_cidrs`; missing levels in between are created","locale":"en"},"9816":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-167","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-set","content":"`<VALUE>`","locale":"en"},"9817":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-168","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-set","content":"The new value. Anything that parses as JSON is taken as JSON (numbers, `true`/`false`, lists, objects), anything else as a string; `null` (or `none`) clears the setting","locale":"en"},"9818":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-169","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-set","content":"Before saving, the whole configuration is checked with the same rules as `check`; if it fails, nothing is written and the reason is reported with exit code 2, for example when listening on a non-local address without allowed networks and a tool access key. On success it prints `<KEY> = <new value>` (`***` for credentials, `(cleared)` when cleared).","locale":"en"},"9819":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-170","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-set","content":"Keep in mind:","locale":"en"},"9820":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-171","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-set","content":"The file is rewritten in Hoshimi's own form. Keys Hoshimi does not know are not saved; the contents of a channel's `accounts` and `options` are kept as they are.","locale":"en"},"9821":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-172","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-set","content":"A value of the wrong type is either refused (for example a `playground.auto_compact` that is not `true` or `false`, or a `server.access_token` that is not a string: exit code 2) or ignored with the old value kept (for example a string for `server.port`), while the command still prints the new value; check with `config get` afterwards.","locale":"en"},"9822":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-173","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-set","content":"Changes apply when the server restarts. Changes made on the Web UI's **Settings** page apply at once (except the listening address and port).","locale":"en"},"9823":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-commands-174","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-commands#config-set","content":"A key typed on the command line stays in your shell history; use the Web UI to set it if that matters.","locale":"en"},"9824":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","type":"page","content":"Environment variables","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Command line"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli-env","locale":"en"},"9825":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-0","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env","content":"Every environment variable Hoshimi reads: its own HOSHIMI_DATA_DIR and HOSHIMI_LOG_LEVEL, the standard variables behind the default data folder and proxies, the credential variables the cloud SDKs read, the variables set for the Playground's commands, and the ones it deliberately ignores.","locale":"en"},"9826":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-1","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimis-own-variables","content":"Hoshimi's own variables","locale":"en"},"9827":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-2","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimi_data_dir","content":"`HOSHIMI_DATA_DIR`","locale":"en"},"9828":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-3","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimi_log_level","content":"`HOSHIMI_LOG_LEVEL`","locale":"en"},"9829":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-4","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli-env#seeing-the-current-values","content":"Seeing the current values","locale":"en"},"9830":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-5","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli-env#system-variables-hoshimi-also-reads","content":"System variables Hoshimi also reads","locale":"en"},"9831":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-6","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli-env#proxy-variables","content":"Proxy variables","locale":"en"},"9832":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-7","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-read-by-the-cloud-sdks","content":"Variables read by the cloud SDKs","locale":"en"},"9833":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-8","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"Variables set for the Playground's commands","locale":"en"},"9834":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-9","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-hoshimi-does-not-read","content":"Variables Hoshimi does not read","locale":"en"},"9835":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-10","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env","content":"Hoshimi's settings live in `config.json`; environment variables decide only two things: **where the data lives** and **how much is logged**. Beyond that, a few standard system variables are read to choose the default data folder and proxies. This page lists them all.","locale":"en"},"9836":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-11","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimis-own-variables","content":"Variable","locale":"en"},"9837":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-12","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimis-own-variables","content":"Default","locale":"en"},"9838":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-13","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimis-own-variables","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"9839":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-14","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimis-own-variables","content":"`HOSHIMI_DATA_DIR`","locale":"en"},"9840":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-15","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimis-own-variables","content":"The platform's user data folder (see below)","locale":"en"},"9841":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-16","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimis-own-variables","content":"The data folder: the configuration file, the database and the runtime file all live here","locale":"en"},"9842":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-17","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimis-own-variables","content":"`HOSHIMI_LOG_LEVEL`","locale":"en"},"9843":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-18","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimis-own-variables","content":"`INFO`","locale":"en"},"9844":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-19","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimis-own-variables","content":"Log level: `DEBUG`, `INFO`, `WARNING` or `ERROR` (case-insensitive)","locale":"en"},"9845":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-20","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimis-own-variables","content":"Every command, `serve` included, reads both.","locale":"en"},"9846":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-21","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimi_data_dir","content":"When set, all of Hoshimi's data moves to this folder together:","locale":"en"},"9847":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-22","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimi_data_dir","content":"File","locale":"en"},"9848":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-23","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimi_data_dir","content":"Content","locale":"en"},"9849":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-24","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimi_data_dir","content":"`config.json`","locale":"en"},"9850":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-25","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimi_data_dir","content":"The configuration, including channel account credentials","locale":"en"},"9851":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-26","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimi_data_dir","content":"`hoshimi.db`","locale":"en"},"9852":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-27","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimi_data_dir"