a different configuration.","locale":"en"},"9871":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-46","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimi_data_dir","content":"The files in the data folder and migration from older releases are covered in Data folder.","locale":"en"},"9872":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-47","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#hoshimi_log_level","content":"Controls Hoshimi's own logging (written to standard error). The `--debug` option has the same effect as `DEBUG`, for that one command:","locale":"en"},"9873":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-48","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#seeing-the-current-values","content":"The first table lists the two variables above with their meaning; when any variable starting with `HOSHIMI_` is set in the current environment, a second table, **Set now**, shows their values (`***` for names containing `TOKEN` or `KEY`). `hoshimi env --json` prints `{\"known\": {…}, \"set\": {…}}`. See the Command reference.","locale":"en"},"9874":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-49","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#system-variables-hoshimi-also-reads","content":"Variable","locale":"en"},"9875":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-50","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#system-variables-hoshimi-also-reads","content":"When it is read","locale":"en"},"9876":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-51","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#system-variables-hoshimi-also-reads","content":"What it does","locale":"en"},"9877":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-52","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#system-variables-hoshimi-also-reads","content":"`XDG_DATA_HOME`","locale":"en"},"9878":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-53","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#system-variables-hoshimi-also-reads","content":"On Linux, when `HOSHIMI_DATA_DIR` is not set","locale":"en"},"9879":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-54","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#system-variables-hoshimi-also-reads","content":"The default data folder becomes `$XDG_DATA_HOME/hoshimi`","locale":"en"},"9880":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-55","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#system-variables-hoshimi-also-reads","content":"`APPDATA`","locale":"en"},"9881":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-56","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#system-variables-hoshimi-also-reads","content":"On Windows, when `HOSHIMI_DATA_DIR` is not set","locale":"en"},"9882":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-57","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#system-variables-hoshimi-also-reads","content":"The default data folder is `%APPDATA%\\hoshimi`","locale":"en"},"9883":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-58","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#system-variables-hoshimi-also-reads","content":"`HTTPS_PROXY`, `HTTP_PROXY`, `ALL_PROXY`, `NO_PROXY`","locale":"en"},"9884":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-59","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#system-variables-hoshimi-also-reads","content":"On every upstream connection while the network mode is `auto` (the default)","locale":"en"},"9885":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-60","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#system-variables-hoshimi-also-reads","content":"Choose a proxy, see below","locale":"en"},"9886":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-61","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#proxy-variables","content":"With the network mode `auto` (the default), Hoshimi reads the proxy variables for each upstream request:","locale":"en"},"9887":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-62","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#proxy-variables","content":"`https://` addresses use `HTTPS_PROXY`, `http://` addresses `HTTP_PROXY`; when that is not set, `ALL_PROXY`.","locale":"en"},"9888":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-63","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#proxy-variables","content":"Hosts listed in `NO_PROXY` are reached directly: host names, domain suffixes, hosts with a port, CIDR networks, or `*` (everything direct), separated by commas or semicolons.","locale":"en"},"9889":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-64","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#proxy-variables","content":"The lowercase forms (`https_proxy` and so on) take precedence over the uppercase ones.","locale":"en"},"9890":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-65","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#proxy-variables","content":"Loopback (this machine) is always reached directly.","locale":"en"},"9891":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-66","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#proxy-variables","content":"A proxy address must be a valid HTTP(S) or SOCKS5 URL; a mistake is reported as an error, not silently ignored.","locale":"en"},"9892":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-67","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#proxy-variables","content":"With no proxy variable at all, `network.system_proxy: true` falls back to the system proxy on Windows.","locale":"en"},"9893":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-68","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#proxy-variables","content":"With the network mode `direct` or `proxy` (a configured proxy), these variables are not read, and `NO_PROXY` applies to automatic mode only. Global and per-channel network settings are in Network and proxies.","locale":"en"},"9894":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-69","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-read-by-the-cloud-sdks","content":"Two cloud platforms leave authentication to the official SDK, which reads environment variables by its own rules:","locale":"en"},"9895":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-70","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-read-by-the-cloud-sdks","content":"**Vertex with `auth: \"adc\"`**: Google's application default credentials (ADC), such as a service account file named by `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS`. Needs `hoshimi[google]`.","locale":"en"},"9896":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-71","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-read-by-the-cloud-sdks","content":"**Amazon Bedrock with AWS default credentials** (no access keys or profile in the account): the AWS SDK's default credential chain, such as `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, `AWS_PROFILE` and the shared configuration files. Needs `hoshimi[bedrock]`.","locale":"en"},"9897":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-72","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-read-by-the-cloud-sdks","content":"These variables must be in the environment of the process that runs Hoshimi, which matters especially for a system service. The account formats are in Cloud platforms.","locale":"en"},"9898":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-73","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"The Playground's **Run commands** and **Background commands** tools add these variables on top of the server process's environment, so command output suits a model and nothing stops to wait for input:","locale":"en"},"9899":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-74","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"Variable","locale":"en"},"9900":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-env-75","page_id":"/en/docs/cli-env","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli-env#variables-set-for-the-playgrounds-commands","content":"Value","locale":"en"},"9901":{"id":