ed-chunk-protocol","content":"`reason`","locale":"en"},"11207":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-127","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#the-normalized-chunk-protocol","content":"`stop`, `tool_calls`, `length` or `error`","locale":"en"},"11208":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-128","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#the-normalized-chunk-protocol","content":"`error`","locale":"en"},"11209":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-129","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#the-normalized-chunk-protocol","content":"`error`","locale":"en"},"11210":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-130","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#the-normalized-chunk-protocol","content":"An error the upstream reported inside the stream","locale":"en"},"11211":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-131","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#the-normalized-chunk-protocol","content":"A typical sequence for one turn:","locale":"en"},"11212":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-132","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#the-normalized-chunk-protocol","content":"On the way out, three pairs of functions turn chunks into the public protocols: `emit_chat_chunks` / `aggregate_chat` (Chat Completions) and `emit_responses_events` / `aggregate_responses` (Responses) in `chunks.py`, and `emit_messages_events` / `aggregate_messages` (Anthropic Messages) in `message_chunks.py`. The rules:","locale":"en"},"11213":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-133","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#the-normalized-chunk-protocol","content":"A `finish.reason` other than `stop`, `tool_calls` or `length` is treated as `stop`; when the upstream sent no `finish`, the output adds a `stop`.","locale":"en"},"11214":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-134","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#the-normalized-chunk-protocol","content":"An `error` chunk becomes an error frame in a stream; without streaming it becomes `UpstreamStreamFailure` and is returned as `upstream_error` (502).","locale":"en"},"11215":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-135","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#the-normalized-chunk-protocol","content":"Once any chunk has gone out, the pool never retries on another account, or the client would receive the content twice.","locale":"en"},"11216":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-136","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#the-normalized-chunk-protocol","content":"OpenAI-compatible stations need not parse their stream: `consume_openai_sse(lines, provider=...)` in `providers/openai_compat.py` turns OpenAI-style SSE into the chunks above, and `read_body` also copes with an upstream that answers a stream request with one whole JSON document. Translation for the other protocols is in `core/translate/` (`anthropic.py`, `gemini.py`, `solo.py`, `responses.py`).","locale":"en"},"11217":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-137","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"An adapter reports an upstream refusal with a `ProviderError` subclass, and the pool decides what comes next by its type:","locale":"en"},"11218":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-138","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"Exception","locale":"en"},"11219":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-139","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"Code","locale":"en"},"11220":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-140","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"What the pool does","locale":"en"},"11221":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-141","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"`AuthFailed`","locale":"en"},"11222":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-142","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"`auth_failed`","locale":"en"},"11223":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-143","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"Renews this account first (once per turn) and retries it on success; otherwise moves to the next account","locale":"en"},"11224":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-144","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"`RefreshTokenRejected`","locale":"en"},"11225":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-145","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"`refresh_token_rejected`","locale":"en"},"11226":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-146","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"The refresh token is spent: the account is marked as needing a new login and leaves the rotation","locale":"en"},"11227":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-147","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"`QuotaExceeded`","locale":"en"},"11228":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-148","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"`quota_exceeded`","locale":"en"},"11229":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-149","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"The account cools down: for the `Retry-After` header's time, else the reset time in the error body, else `quota_hold_seconds`; next account","locale":"en"},"11230":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-150","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"`PolicyBlocked`","locale":"en"},"11231":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-151","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"`policy_blocked`","locale":"en"},"11232":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-152","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"The account cools down for `policy_block_seconds`, without renewal; next account","locale":"en"},"11233":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-153","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"`ModelSaturated`","locale":"en"},"11234":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-154","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"`model_saturated`","locale":"en"},"11235":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-155","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"The model itself is overloaded, for every account alike: stop at once and hand the station's words to the caller","locale":"en"},"11236":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-156","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"`ModelGone`","locale":"en"},"11237":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-157","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"`model_gone`","locale":"en"},"11238":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-158","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"Keep asking the other accounts; when all of them say so, the registry marks the model dead","locale":"en"},"11239":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-159","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"Any other `ProviderError`","locale":"en"},"11240":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-160","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"`upstream_error`","locale":"en"},"11241":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-161","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"Next account when the status is recoverable; otherwise (a problem with the caller's own request) stop at once","locale":"en"},"11242":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-162","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"When every account has been tried and the last error is the kind that time may change, the pool makes up to `backoff_retries` more passes: it waits for the time the upstream named (at most `backoff_max_seconds`), or a random wait (full jitter) when none was named. Once content has gone out, it never retries.","locale":"en"},"11243":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-163","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"`raise_for_status(response, provider=...)` in `openai_compat.py` classifies an HTTP answer in a fixed order: first whether the model does not exist (404/410 and the like), then model saturation, safety block, 401/403 authentication failure, 403 permission denied, and quota (402/429, or quota wording in the body). The order matters: a saturated model often arrives as a plain 429 and a safety block as a plain 403, and read by status alone they would pass for a spent allowance or a bad credential. An error frame inside a 200 stream becomes an exception only for \"model gone\", saturation, a block or quota; anything else is yielded to the caller as an `error` chunk.","locale":"en"},"11244":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-164","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"The dead-model record (`DeadModelStore` in `failure.py`) lives in memory only: one strike is forgotten after 10 minutes; three strikes within that window make an entry that time no longer lifts. The model's next answer that yields a first chunk clears it.","locale":"en"},"11245":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-165","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#errors-and-account-rotation","content":"The `on_route(provider_id, account_id, attempt)` callback of `stream_using` fires when an account yields its first chunk, so usage records the account that actually answered.","locale":"en"},"11246":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-166","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#catalogues-and-capabilities","content":"`Provider.models()` manages the catalogue cache; an adapter implements only `fetch_models()`:","locale":"en"},"11247":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-167","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#catalogues-and-capabilities","content":"A successful catalogue is cached for 300 seconds.","locale":"en"},"11248":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-168","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#catalogues-and-capabilities","content":"When fetching fails, the previous result is kept and fetching is retried after 30 seconds; with no earlier success, `fallback_models()` is used.","locale":"en"},"11249":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-169","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#catalogues-and-capabilities","content":"A new catalogue less than half the size of the previous one is treated as a partial answer and the old one is kept for one cycle; if the next cycle says the same, it is accepted.","locale":"en"},"11250":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-170","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#catalogues-and-capabilities","content":"`fetch_models()` sets `catalog_authoritative = True` when it got a catalogue (`OpenAiCompatProvider` already does), so an empty catalogue from the station counts as its real answer rather than falling back to the fixed list.","locale":"en"},"11251":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-171","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#catalogues-and-capabilities","content":"`specs()` returns each model's `ModelSpec` (`hoshimi/core/catalog.py`), which the reasoning-effort policy and `GET /api/v1/models` read:","locale":"en"},"11252":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-172","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#catalogues-and-capabilities","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"11253":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-173","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#catalogues-and-capabilities","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"11254":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-174","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#catalogues-and-capabilities","content":"`wire`","locale":"en"},"11255":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-175","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#catalogues-and-capabilities","content":"The protocol sent upstream: `chat`, `messages`, `responses` and so on","locale":"en"},"11256":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-176","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#catalogues-and-capabilities","content":"`vision`, `reasoning`, `tools`","locale":"en"},"11257":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-177","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#catalogues-and-capabilities","content":"Takes images, thinks, supports tools (`tools` is `None` when unknown)","locale":"en"},"11258":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-178","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#catalogues-and-capabilities","content":"`context_window`, `max_output`","locale":"en"},"11259":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-179","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#catalogues-and-capabilities","content":"Context and output limits; 131072 and 32768 when unknown","locale":"en"},"11260":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-180","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#catalogues-and-capabilities","content":"`free`","locale":"en"},"11261":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-181","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#catalogues-and-capabilities","content":"Whether calling it costs nothing; three-way, with `None` for \"the station did not say\"","locale":"en"},"11262":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-182","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#catalogues-and-capabilities","content":"`efforts`, `effort_default`, `effort_off_id`, `effort_patch`, `effort_off_patch`","locale":"en"},"11263":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-183","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#catalogues-and-capabilities","content":"The model's own reasoning-effort choices and how they are written on the wire","locale":"en"},"11264":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-184","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#catalogues-and-capabilities","content":"`can_disable_thinking`, `region_sensitive`","locale":"en"},"11265":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-185","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#catalogues-and-capabilities","content":"Whether thinking can be switched off, whether the region matters","locale":"en"},"11266":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-186","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#catalogues-and-capabilities","content":"Each station's capability table is in `catalog.py` (`zhipu_spec`, `kilo_spec`, `cline_spec` and so on). The default `specs()` gives every model an inert spec (no reasoning, so the effort policy leaves request bodies alone), then fills in \"reasons\" and \"takes images\" from models.dev, never overriding what a table already says. How reasoning effort behaves is in Model behaviour.","locale":"en"},"11267":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-187","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#writing-a-dedicated-adapter","content":"Taking the Zhipu GLM provider (`providers/zhipu.py`), an OpenAI-compatible station, as the example:","locale":"en"},"11268":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-188","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#write-the-adapter-class","content":"An OpenAI-compatible station subclasses `OpenAiCompatProvider`, declares only its address, catalogue path and fixed list, and overrides the headers, body or catalogue parsing where needed:","locale":"en"},"11269":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-189","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#write-the-adapter-class","content":"`OpenAiCompatProvider.stream_raw` does the rest: it builds the body (`build_body`, forcing `stream: true`), records the upstream's quota headers, calls `raise_for_status` on an error and converts the stream with `consume_openai_sse`. A station whose protocol is not OpenAI's subclasses `Provider` directly and implements `stream_raw` itself, with the translation helpers in `core/translate/`.","locale":"en"},"11270":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-190","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#register-it","content":"In `providers/factory.py`, add the class to `PROVIDER_CLASSES` and put the ID at the right place in `PROVIDER_ORDER`. That order decides which provider a bare model name is looked up in first, and the order keyless providers start in.","locale":"en"},"11271":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-191","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#write-the-capability-table","content":"In `catalog.py`, write a `<id>_spec(model_id, provider)` for the station, with context, images, thinking and reasoning-effort choices.","locale":"en"},"11272":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-192","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#describe-the-account-form","content":"In `credential_forms()` of `core/provider_forms.py`, say which fields adding an account asks for (`zhipu` needs only `api_key`). The Web UI's **Add account** dialog and the management API both read it; list only fields the adapter actually accepts.","locale":"en"},"11273":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-193","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#write-tests","content":"Replace the upstream with `httpx.MockTransport` and check where the request went, what it carried, and the chunks that came out:","locale":"en"},"11274":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-194","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#write-tests","content":"The test layout and shared fixtures are in Testing.","locale":"en"},"11275":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-195","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#update-the-documentation","content":"Describe how to sign in, what the provider offers and its limits on Free stations or the matching provider page, in both languages. When the provider comes from a reference project, record it in `core/provider_sources.py` and run `python scripts/generate_provider_inventory.py` to regenerate the Provider inventory.","locale":"en"},"11276":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-196","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#adding-a-service-defined-as-data","content":"A service that needs only an API key and speaks a plain protocol needs no class: one line in `CANONICAL_PROVIDERS` of `core/provider_definitions.py` is enough, for example:","locale":"en"},"11277":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-197","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#adding-a-service-defined-as-data","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"11278":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-198","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#adding-a-service-defined-as-data","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"11279":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-199","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#adding-a-service-defined-as-data","content":"`id`, `name`, `base_url`","locale":"en"},"11280":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-200","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#adding-a-service-defined-as-data","content":"The provider ID, the name shown, the API root","locale":"en"},"11281":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-201","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#adding-a-service-defined-as-data","content":"`protocol`","locale":"en"},"11282":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-202","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#adding-a-service-defined-as-data","content":"`chat`, `messages`, `responses`, `multi` (chosen per model) and others","locale":"en"},"11283":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-203","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#adding-a-service-defined-as-data","content":"`auth`","locale":"en"},"11284":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-204","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#adding-a-service-defined-as-data","content":"Supported authentication, such as `(\"api_key\",)` or `(\"api_key\", \"oauth\")`","locale":"en"},"11285":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-205","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#adding-a-service-defined-as-data","content":"`plan`","locale":"en"},"11286":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-206","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#adding-a-service-defined-as-data","content":"The plan, which tells apart different services at the same address","locale":"en"},"11287":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-207","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#adding-a-service-defined-as-data","content":"`catalog`","locale":"en"},"11288":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-208","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#adding-a-service-defined-as-data","content":"The catalogue path (used as `models_path` when it starts with `/` and has no space), or a note on where the catalogue comes from","locale":"en"},"11289":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-209","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#adding-a-service-defined-as-data","content":"`adapter`","locale":"en"},"11290":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-210","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#adding-a-service-defined-as-data","content":"`configured` (class generated), `dedicated` (has its own adapter) or `local`","locale":"en"},"11291":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-211","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#adding-a-service-defined-as-data","content":"`implemented`","locale":"en"},"11292":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-212","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#adding-a-service-defined-as-data","content":"Whether it is implemented; unimplemented ones are not registered","locale":"en"},"11293":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-213","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#adding-a-service-defined-as-data","content":"`key_env`","locale":"en"},"11294":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-214","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#adding-a-service-defined-as-data","content":"The environment variable the reference project reads the key from; a record only, Hoshimi does not read it","locale":"en"},"11295":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-215","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#adding-a-service-defined-as-data","content":"A `configured` service gets a `ConfiguredProvider` subclass from `regular_provider_classes()`, and `provider_forms.py` gives every service that supports `api_key` an \"API key + address + models\" form automatically. A service with an unusual catalogue endpoint is described in `providers/catalog_profiles.py`; one whose request body needs adjusting, in `providers/request_profiles.py`. `tests/core/test_provider_definitions.py` checks that different services of one brand are not merged because they share a name or an address.","locale":"en"},"11296":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-216","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#interactive-logins","content":"A station that needs a browser login or a device code gets a login flow in `core/login/`. The command line's `hoshimi login <id>` and the Web UI's login dialog share it.","locale":"en"},"11297":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-217","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#the-contract","content":"A flow receives an HTTP client and a `report` callback. The moment the station gives a browser address, the flow must call `report(url)`: the command line prints it and opens a browser, the API hands it to the Web UI, and neither needs to know whether the station used a device code, an external login link or a local callback port. The flow then blocks until the credential is ready and returns the account dictionary the provider understands; on failure it raises `LoginError`, whose message is shown to the user as is.","locale":"en"},"11298":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-218","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#the-contract","content":"`report` is a `LoginReporter`, which also offers:","locale":"en"},"11299":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-219","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#the-contract","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"11300":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-220","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#the-contract","content":"Used for","locale":"en"},"11301":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-221","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#the-contract","content":"`report.device_code(url, code, expires_in)`","locale":"en"},"11302":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-222","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#the-contract","content":"Device-code flows: reports the address, the code the user enters and how long it lasts","locale":"en"},"11303":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-223","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#the-contract","content":"`report.authorization(server, timeout)`","locale":"en"},"11304":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-224","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#the-contract","content":"Waits for the local callback, while letting the user paste the final redirect URL or the authorization code","locale":"en"},"11305":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-225","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#the-contract","content":"`report.wait(seconds)`","locale":"en"},"11306":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-226","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#the-contract","content":"The polling pause; raises `LoginError` when the login was cancelled","locale":"en"},"11307":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-227","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#the-contract","content":"`report.check_cancelled()`","locale":"en"},"11308":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-228","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#the-contract","content":"Checks whether the login was cancelled","locale":"en"},"11309":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-229","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#the-contract","content":"`report.on_commit(action)`","locale":"en"},"11310":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-230","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#the-contract","content":"Defers the flow's own local writes until the login is confirmed","locale":"en"},"11311":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-231","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#the-contract","content":"`LOGIN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` is 600 seconds; the manager gives the whole flow 60 seconds more, so the flow's own timeout fires first.","locale":"en"},"11312":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-232","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#example-kilos-device-code-login","content":"(Abridged; see `hoshimi/core/login/kilo.py`.) Kilo returns a long-lived key, so the flow invents no `refresh_token` or `expires_at`, which would schedule renewals that do not exist.","locale":"en"},"11313":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-233","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#registering-and-writing-back","content":"Add `\"<id>\": start_<id>_login` to `_flows()` in `core/login/manager.py` (flows are imported lazily there, so one station's problem cannot break startup). `LoginManager` does the rest:","locale":"en"},"11314":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-234","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#registering-and-writing-back","content":"Each login is a session (`pending`, `succeeded`, `failed`) that runs on a background thread and is dropped an hour after it started; a session can be cancelled, and one waiting for an authorization code accepts one.","locale":"en"},"11315":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-235","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#registering-and-writing-back","content":"On success, the credential is written to the provider's `accounts` in `config.json` and the provider is enabled. When the credential carries a stable identity (the first of `user_id`, `account_id`, `userid`, `uid`, `sub`, `access_key_id`, `api_key`, `access_token`), logging in again as the same identity replaces the account instead of adding another.","locale":"en"},"11316":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-236","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#registering-and-writing-back","content":"Right after the write, the provider pool is rebuilt from the new configuration, so the new account is usable at once.","locale":"en"},"11317":{"id":"/en/docs/development-providers-237","page_id":"/en/docs/development-providers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-providers#registering-and-writing-back","content":"For a credential that needs renewing, implement `refresh_account` in the adapter. The timer in `refresh.py` sweeps every account every 30 minutes, renews those within an hour of their recorded expiry (and, every time, those with no recorded expiry), and writes back to `config.json` only the account that changed.","locale":"en"},"11318":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","type":"page","content":"CI and releases","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-release","locale":"en"},"11319":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-0","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-release","content":"Where the version lives, how the wheel gets the built Web UI and is checked, what each of the four CI workflows does, how one push publishes a new version to PyPI and GitHub, and how the docs site is deployed.","locale":"en"},"11320":{"id":"/en/docs/development-release-1","page_id":"/en/docs/development-release","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/development-release#the-version","content":"The version","locale":"en"},"11321":{"id":"/en/docs/developm