06":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-71","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#common-patterns","content":"**Anthropic Messages**: `tests/api/test_native_messages.py` drives the gateway with the official Anthropic SDK's JSON and stream helpers (the SDK is in the `dev` extra), against a local mock transport, so no real credentials are needed. `tests/api/test_messages_heartbeat.py` separately checks the heartbeat timing, that heartbeats never split a whole SSE frame, and that the upstream is released when the client goes away. To try a configured gateway with real Claude Code, see Claude Code.","locale":"en"},"11707":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-72","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#common-patterns","content":"**POSIX-only tests**: the Playground's shell and background-command tests skip on Windows (`pytest.mark.skipif(os.name == \"nt\", ...)`); usage tests that switch the local time zone skip where `time.tzset` is missing.","locale":"en"},"11708":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-73","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#common-patterns","content":"**Your own Services**: call `make_services(default_model=..., ...)` for particular settings; pass extra `FakeProvider`s or subclasses for several providers.","locale":"en"},"11709":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-74","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#web-ui-tests","content":"In `hoshimi/webui`, `bun run test` runs Vitest and `bun run typecheck` runs vue-tsc; `python scripts/dev.py test-web` runs both in turn. The environment is happy-dom; `src/test/setup.ts` supplies the `ElementInternals` that `@material/web` asks for, and `src/test/motion-zero.css` sets every motion duration to zero, so a test never waits on a transition. Vitest uses the `vmThreads` pool (worker threads race each other creating their temporary folder on Windows).","locale":"en"},"11710":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-75","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#web-ui-tests","content":"Tests sit next to the files they test (`*.test.ts`). Besides the component, store and query tests, a few suites check rules that apply everywhere:","locale":"en"},"11711":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-76","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#web-ui-tests","content":"Test","locale":"en"},"11712":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-77","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#web-ui-tests","content":"Rule","locale":"en"},"11713":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-78","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#web-ui-tests","content":"`src/layout.test.ts`","locale":"en"},"11714":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-79","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#web-ui-tests","content":"The layout rules: rows that can shrink, bounded lists, scrolling only through `.app-scroll`, scrollbar lanes, the bottom navigation, unstretched charts; see Web UI","locale":"en"},"11715":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-80","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#web-ui-tests","content":"`src/tokens.test.ts`","locale":"en"},"11716":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-81","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#web-ui-tests","content":"No hex colours in `.vue` and `.css` outside `src/theme/`","locale":"en"},"11717":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-82","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#web-ui-tests","content":"`src/imports.test.ts`","locale":"en"},"11718":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-83","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#web-ui-tests","content":"Modules import each other through the `@/` alias, with no relative path","locale":"en"},"11719":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-84","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#web-ui-tests","content":"`src/i18n/i18n.test.ts`","locale":"en"},"11720":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-85","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#web-ui-tests","content":"English, Simplified Chinese and Japanese have the same keys and placeholders; system language detection","locale":"en"},"11721":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-86","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#web-ui-tests","content":"`src/devProxy.test.ts`","locale":"en"},"11722":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-87","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#web-ui-tests","content":"The dev proxy shortens only the \"API is not up\" kind of error to one line; anything else is still printed in full","locale":"en"},"11723":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-88","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#web-ui-tests","content":"`src/ui/layers.test.ts`, `src/ui/motion/motion.test.ts` and others","locale":"en"},"11724":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-89","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#web-ui-tests","content":"Layer stacking and focus, the motion helpers","locale":"en"},"11725":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-90","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#the-generated-type-check","content":"`python scripts/dev.py typegen-check` regenerates `hoshimi/webui/src/api/schema.d.ts` from the current code and compares it with `git diff --exit-code`. A failure means a management API model changed without the types being regenerated: run `python scripts/dev.py typegen` and commit `schema.d.ts`.","locale":"en"},"11726":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-91","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#checking-the-layout-in-browsers-check_layoutpy","content":"Every scrolling area in the Web UI scrolls in one direction (`.app-scroll` down, `.app-scroll-x` sideways, such as code blocks, tables and the stepper), so a sideways scrollbar anywhere else is a layout bug. The unit tests can only read the source; `scripts/check_layout.py` finds these bugs in real browsers.","locale":"en"},"11727":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-92","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#checking-the-layout-in-browsers-check_layoutpy","content":"Start a server first (`hoshimi serve` or `python scripts/dev.py dev`), ideally with a conversation in the Playground, so the chat list, the editor and the menus have something to open. The script:","locale":"en"},"11728":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-93","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#checking-the-layout-in-browsers-check_layoutpy","content":"opens `/overview`, `/models`, `/channels`, `/usage`, `/playground` and `/settings` in turn;","locale":"en"},"11729":{"id":"/en/docs/development-testing-94","page_id":"/en/docs/development-testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/development-testing#checking-the-layout-in-browsers-check_layoutpy","content":"checks them in Chromium (with its scrollbars shown, as on a desktop) and Firefox (whose scrollbars float), at window widths of 320, 360, 600, 900, 1280 and 1600 pixels;","locale":