r most, Responses for `openai`, `meta`, `xai` and `codex`, Anthropic Messages for `anthropic`, `minimax-api`, `minimax-cn` and `vercel-ai-gateway`. \"Multi\" channels choose per model:","locale":"en"},"14879":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-96","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#protocols","content":"`github-copilot` picks Responses, Messages or Chat from the endpoints the catalogue lists for the model.","locale":"en"},"14880":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-97","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#protocols","content":"In `fireworks` and `opencode-go`, models whose name starts with `claude` use Messages; in `opencode-go`, models starting with `gemini-` use the native Gemini protocol.","locale":"en"},"14881":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-98","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#protocols","content":"Everything else defaults to Chat. The account's `protocol` or `options.model_protocols` overrides this.","locale":"en"},"14882":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-99","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#protocols","content":"When the upstream speaks Anthropic Messages, `/v1/messages` requests from Anthropic clients (such as Claude Code) are passed through natively, without format conversion. Feature boundaries and client setup are in Anthropic API.","locale":"en"},"14883":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-100","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#compatibility-handling","content":"Hoshimi adjusts requests for each service's known differences, for example:","locale":"en"},"14884":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-101","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#compatibility-handling","content":"In Chat requests, `max_completion_tokens` becomes `max_tokens` (`minimax-chat` and `wandb` use `max_completion_tokens` instead); services that do not accept the `developer` role get `system`.","locale":"en"},"14885":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-102","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#compatibility-handling","content":"`deepseek` gets `reasoning_content` filled in on past assistant messages; `mistral` and `mistral-codestral` turn tool-call IDs into 9-character alphanumeric IDs; `cohere` drops the fields it does not support and `name` on messages.","locale":"en"},"14886":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-103","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#compatibility-handling","content":"Services that reject certain fields have `store`, `reasoning_effort` or tool-definition `strict` removed.","locale":"en"},"14887":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-104","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#compatibility-handling","content":"`openrouter` reads its catalogue from `/models/user`, falling back to `/models` when refused.","locale":"en"},"14888":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-105","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#compatibility-handling","content":"How thinking levels are sent differs by service (a menu appears only when the catalogue says the model thinks):","locale":"en"},"14889":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-106","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#compatibility-handling","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"14890":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-107","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#compatibility-handling","content":"Channels","locale":"en"},"14891":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-108","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#compatibility-ha