":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#built-in-services","content":"api","locale":"en"},"15182":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-399","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#built-in-services","content":"`codex` (ChatGPT subscription sign-in) is in Free stations; the cloud platforms and NVIDIA are in Cloud platforms and NVIDIA NIM. The sources behind these services are mapped in the provider inventory.","locale":"en"},"15183":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-local-400","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-local","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-local#when-to-use-agg-instead","content":"When the service is in the table above, use its channel: it carries the service's protocol, catalogue endpoint and compatibility rules. When it is not, but speaks OpenAI Chat Completions, use agg: put the address and key in an account, and one agg channel can hold several stations.","locale":"en"},"15184":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","type":"page","content":"NVIDIA NIM","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Providers"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","locale":"en"},"15185":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-0","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","content":"Connect NVIDIA-hosted NIM models with an API key: adding the account, choosing models, catalogue filtering, and the request translations the adapter makes for NIM.","locale":"en"},"15186":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-1","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#adding-an-account","content":"Adding an account","locale":"en"},"15187":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-2","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#choosing-a-model","content":"Choosing a model","locale":"en"},"15188":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-3","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#catalogue","content":"Catalogue","locale":"en"},"15189":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-4","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#request-translations","content":"Request translations","locale":"en"},"15190":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-5","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","content":"The `nvidia` channel connects to NVIDIA's hosted NIM inference service (`https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1`) over OpenAI Chat Completions. An account needs only an NVIDIA API key.","locale":"en"},"15191":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-6","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#adding-an-account","content":"Open **Channels** › **NVIDIA NIM**, click **Add account**, enter the **API key** and click **Save account**. The account takes effect immediately.","locale":"en"},"15192":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-7","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#adding-an-account","content":"Find the configuration file with `hoshimi config path` and add:","locale":"en"},"15193":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-8","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#adding-an-account","content":"Restart after editing the file.","locale":"en"},"15194":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-9","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#adding-an-account","content":"The account also accepts `access_token` in place of `api_key`, and `models` on the account declares a model list in place of the live catalogue; the channel option `options.base_url` replaces the default address. This upstream key is a different thing from the gateway's own model API key and management key; see Security.","locale":"en"},"15195":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-10","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#choosing-a-model","content":"Use `nvidia/<model-id>` to select this channel explicitly. When the model ID itself contains a slash, the `nvidia/` prefix makes sure the request lands here rather than on an earlier channel in the routing order:","locale":"en"},"15196":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-11","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#catalogue","content":"The adapter reads the model list live and excludes recognised non-chat tasks: embeddings (`embed`), rerankers (`rerank`), `nvclip`, reward scorers (`-reward`), detectors (`-detector`), document parsers (`nemotron-parse`) and `gliner`. This is a task filter, not an outage list.","locale":"en"},"15197":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-12","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#catalogue","content":"A model being listed does not prove there is quota for it or that inference will succeed. `nvidia` takes part in the default availability probe, so you can confirm with one real request from the **Models** page or `POST /api/v1/probe`; see Model behaviour. Capability metadata and account options follow the same model rules.","locale":"en"},"15198":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-13","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#request-translations","content":"NIM does not accept some OpenAI fields, so the adapter changes requests before sending them:","locale":"en"},"15199":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-14","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#request-translations","content":"Translation","locale":"en"},"15200":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-15","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#request-translations","content":"Details","locale":"en"},"15201":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-16","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#request-translations","content":"Removed fields","locale":"en"},"15202":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-17","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#request-translations","content":"`store`, `reasoning_effort`, `reasoning`, `prompt_cache_retention`","locale":"en"},"15203":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-18","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#request-translations","content":"`max_completion_tokens`","locale":"en"},"15204":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-19","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#request-translations","content":"Becomes `max_tokens` when no `max_tokens` was given","locale":"en"},"15205":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-20","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#request-translations","content":"`developer` messages","locale":"en"},"15206":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-21","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#request-translations","content":"Become `system`","locale":"en"},"15207":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-22","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#request-translations","content":"Tool definitions","locale":"en"},"15208":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-23","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#request-translations","content":"`strict` is removed; boolean sub-schemas such as `additionalProperties` or `items`, and boolean properties, are cleaned out of parameter schemas","locale":"en"},"15209":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-24","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#request-translations","content":"Tool calls from MiniMax models","locale":"en"},"15210":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-25","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#request-translations","content":"Tool calls the model writes as native text blocks are parsed into standard tool calls","locale":"en"},"15211":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-26","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#request-translations","content":"Request header","locale":"en"},"15212":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-27","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#request-translations","content":"`NVCF-POLL-SECONDS: 3600` is sent","locale":"en"},"15213":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-28","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#request-translations","content":"These translations make requests acceptable to NIM; they are not full OpenAI feature parity. Whether a request succeeds is finally decided by the key's permissions, quota and model access.","locale":"en"},"15214":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia-29","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-nvidia#request-translations","content":"Client setup is in Connecting clients; general account handling is in Provider concepts.","locale":"en"},"15215":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","type":"page","content":"Free stations","breadcrumbs":["Hoshimi Documentation","Providers"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-stations","locale":"en"},"15216":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-0","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations","content":"How to use each sign-in station adapter: Cline, Gemini Code Assist, ZCode, MiniMax, TRAE, Qoder, CodeBuddy/WorkBuddy, CodeArts, Loomy, Raccoon, LobsterAI, Codex, EAC and Zhipu — how to sign in, what each offers and its limits.","locale":"en"},"15217":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-1","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#signing-in","content":"Signing in","locale":"en"},"15218":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-2","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#at-a-glance","content":"At a glance","locale":"en"},"15219":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-3","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#cline-cline","content":"Cline (`cline`)","locale":"en"},"15220":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-4","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#gemini-code-assist-gemini","content":"Gemini Code Assist (`gemini`)","locale":"en"},"15221":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-5","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#zcode-zcode","content":"ZCode (`zcode`)","locale":"en"},"15222":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-6","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#minimax-minimax","content":"MiniMax (`minimax`)","locale":"en"},"15223":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-7","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"TRAE (`trae`)","locale":"en"},"15224":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-8","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#qoder-qoder-qodercn","content":"Qoder (`qoder`, `qodercn`)","locale":"en"},"15225":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-9","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#qoder-cli-qodercli-qodercli-cn","content":"Qoder CLI (`qodercli`, `qodercli-cn`)","locale":"en"},"15226":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-10","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#codebuddy--workbuddy-buddy-workbuddy","content":"CodeBuddy / WorkBuddy (`buddy`, `workbuddy`)","locale":"en"},"15227":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-11","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#codearts-codearts","content":"CodeArts (`codearts`)","locale":"en"},"15228":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-12","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#loomy-loomy","content":"Loomy (`loomy`)","locale":"en"},"15229":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-13","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#raccoon-raccoon","content":"Raccoon (`raccoon`)","locale":"en"},"15230":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-14","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#lobsterai-lobsterai","content":"LobsterAI (`lobsterai`)","locale":"en"},"15231":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-15","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#codex-codex","content":"Codex (`codex`)","locale":"en"},"15232":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-16","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#eac-eac","content":"EAC (`eac`)","locale":"en"},"15233":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-17","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#zhipu-zhipu","content":"Zhipu (`zhipu`)","locale":"en"},"15234":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-18","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#renewal-check-in-and-balances","content":"Renewal, check-in and balances","locale":"en"},"15235":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-19","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#other-channels-with-sign-in","content":"Other channels with sign-in","locale":"en"},"15236":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-20","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations","content":"These channels correspond to the free, trial or subscription allowances of AI coding tools and platforms. Most of these stations do not hand out an API key you can paste; they issue tokens through a browser sign-in. Hoshimi performs the sign-in in place of the official client, stores the credential as an account, and takes care of renewal and check-in.","locale":"en"},"15237":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-21","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations","content":"This page describes what Hoshimi's adapters implement. Each station decides its own free allowance, models and rules, and can change them at any time; the built-in model lists are only a fallback for when the station's listing cannot be reached. What actually works is whatever the station answers now.","locale":"en"},"15238":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-22","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#signing-in","content":"Open **Channels** and pick the station from the list (stations without accounts are under the **Not set up** filter).","locale":"en"},"15239":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-23","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#signing-in","content":"Click **Sign in**. The dialog goes through **Request a link**, **Finish in the browser** and **Signed in**, and opens the station's login page in a new tab.","locale":"en"},"15240":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-24","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#signing-in","content":"For device-code stations, the dialog shows a **Verification code**; enter it on the authorization page.","locale":"en"},"15241":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-25","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#signing-in","content":"When the browser is not on the machine running Hoshimi, paste the address the browser finally lands on into **Authorization code or callback URL** and click **Submit code**.","locale":"en"},"15242":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-26","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#signing-in","content":"On success it prints `Signed into <channel> as <account id>.` and the account is written to `config.json`.","locale":"en"},"15243":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-27","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#signing-in","content":"A sign-in waits at most 10 minutes. In the Web UI you can cancel it; a callback that arrives after cancelling does not save an account.","locale":"en"},"15244":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-28","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#signing-in","content":"Signing in again as the same station identity updates the existing account rather than adding another.","locale":"en"},"15245":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-29","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#signing-in","content":"Stations that need a local callback listen only on `127.0.0.1` (or `localhost`) for the duration of the sign-in, never on a public interface. When the browser is on another machine, paste the callback with `--manual` or the Web UI's **Authorization code or callback URL**. The one flow without manual input (Loomy) has to be finished in a browser on the same machine.","locale":