docs/providers-stations-128","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#cline-cline","content":"**Sign-in**: `hoshimi login cline` uses WorkOS device authorization by default, then registers with Cline to obtain the station token. The token is stored with its `workos:` prefix and sent as is.","locale":"en"},"15345":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-129","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#cline-cline","content":"**Login method**: the channel's **Network** section has a **Cline login method** selector with **Device code (SDK)** (default) and **Browser (extension)**, matching `sdk` and `extension` for `providers.cline.options.client_profile`. The extension flow takes a callback on one of the local ports 48801–48811 and accepts a pasted callback. New accounts record the method they signed in with; changing the selector affects later sign-ins only.","locale":"en"},"15346":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-130","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#cline-cline","content":"**Balance**: needs the account's `account_id` (a `usr-…` value, saved automatically at sign-in).","locale":"en"},"15347":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-131","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#cline-cline","content":"**Account fields**: `access_token`, `refresh_token`, `client_profile`, `account_id`.","locale":"en"},"15348":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-132","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#gemini-code-assist-gemini","content":"Google's Code Assist lane (`daily-cloudcode-pa.googleapis.com`), signed in with a Google account. It is a different service from the Gemini Developer API (`google`) and Vertex AI (`google-vertex`); see Cloud platforms.","locale":"en"},"15349":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-133","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#gemini-code-assist-gemini","content":"**Sign-in**: `hoshimi login gemini` opens Google's consent page, which calls back to a temporary port on `localhost`; a pasted callback is accepted. The sign-in stores the public desktop client's `client_id` and `client_secret` with the account, so renewal needs no extra setup. `options.client_id` / `options.client_secret` override them.","locale":"en"},"15350":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-134","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#gemini-code-assist-gemini","content":"**Models**: a single `gemini-3.8-flash`, with thinking levels `low`, `medium`, `high` and `tiered` (`medium` when none is given). The level sets the thinking budget and is appended to the upstream model name as a suffix.","locale":"en"},"15351":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-135","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#gemini-code-assist-gemini","content":"**Balance**: shows the remaining share of the five-hour and weekly quota windows, not credits.","locale":"en"},"15352":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-136","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#zcode-zcode","content":"The free-plan lane of Zhipu's ZCode client, using the Anthropic Messages protocol. The models are `GLM-5.3-Flash` and `GLM-5.3`, with thinking levels `low`, `high` and `max`, sent as `output_config.effort`.","locale":"en"},"15353":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-137","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#zcode-zcode","content":"**Sign-in**: `hoshimi login zcode` is mediated by the station and authorised with a Zhipu account; there is no local callback, so it works on a remote server. The sign-in generates and stores a fixed `device_mid`.","locale":"en"},"15354":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-138","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#zcode-zcode","content":"**Renewal**: the adapter does not renew; sign in again when the token stops working.","locale":"en"},"15355":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-139","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#zcode-zcode","content":"**Note**: the adapter puts the official ZCode client's identity and environment sections before the caller's system prompt, and inserts a date reminder before the first user message. The caller's system prompt is kept, after those blocks.","locale":"en"},"15356":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-140","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#zcode-zcode","content":"**Options**: `options.app_version` (default `3.14.3`).","locale":"en"},"15357":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-141","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#zcode-zcode","content":"**Account fields**: `zcode_jwt` (or `access_token`), `device_mid`.","locale":"en"},"15358":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-142","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#minimax-minimax","content":"The MiniMax Agent sign-in lane (Anthropic Messages protocol), unrelated to the key-billed `minimax-api`, `minimax-cn` and `minimax-chat`.","locale":"en"},"15359":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-143","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#minimax-minimax","content":"**Sign-in**: `hoshimi login minimax` uses a device code on `account.minimax.cn`, checked with PKCE.","locale":"en"},"15360":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-144","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#minimax-minimax","content":"**Models**: `MiniMax-M3.1-Flash-Preview`, `MiniMax-M3`, `MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed`, `MiniMax-M2.7`. The M3.1 family requires adaptive thinking, so the adapter turns it on even when no level is given; M2.7 declares no levels, so a caller's level is not forwarded.","locale":"en"},"15361":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-145","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#minimax-minimax","content":"**Check-in and balance**: daily credits are claimed by the UTC+8 calendar day; the balance is the sum of what remains in each credit pack.","locale":"en"},"15362":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-146","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#minimax-minimax","content":"**Account fields**: `access_token`, `refresh_token`.","locale":"en"},"15363":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-147","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"ByteDance TRAE's SOLO lane, China edition (`api.trae.com.cn`, `trae-api-cn.mchost.guru`).","locale":"en"},"15364":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-148","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"**Sign-in**: `hoshimi login trae` opens the login page on `www.trae.cn`; the station sends the tokens straight back to a local callback, on port 18080 when free or any free port otherwise. A pasted callback is accepted.","locale":"en"},"15365":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-149","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"**Models**: the fallback list includes `DeepSeek-V4-Flash-Official`, `Doubao-Seed-2.1-Pro`, `glm-5.2`, `kimi-k3` and others. TRAE provides a context-length table but no thinking menu, so a caller's `reasoning_effort` is forwarded unchanged.","locale":"en"},"15366":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-150","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"**Check-in and balance**: the device identity is derived from the account's `uid`; an account without `uid` cannot check in.","locale":"en"},"15367":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-151","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"**Account fields**: `access_token`, `refresh_token`, `device_id`, `machine_id`, `uid`.","locale":"en"},"15368":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-152","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"Option","locale":"en"},"15369":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-153","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"Default","locale":"en"},"15370":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-154","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"15371":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-155","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"`channel`","locale":"en"},"15372":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-156","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"`solo_work_lite`","locale":"en"},"15373":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-157","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"The feature channel requests use","locale":"en"},"15374":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-158","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"`user_agent`","locale":"en"},"15375":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-159","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"`Trae/0.1.52`","locale":"en"},"15376":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-160","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"User-Agent","locale":"en"},"15377":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-161","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"`app_id`","locale":"en"},"15378":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-162","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"built-in value","locale":"en"},"15379":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-163","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"`X-App-Id`","locale":"en"},"15380":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-164","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"`ide_version`","locale":"en"},"15381":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-165","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"`0.1.52`","locale":"en"},"15382":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-166","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"`X-Ide-Version`","locale":"en"},"15383":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-167","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"`ide_version_code`","locale":"en"},"15384":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-168","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"`20260811`","locale":"en"},"15385":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-169","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"`X-Ide-Version-Code`","locale":"en"},"15386":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-170","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"`os_version`","locale":"en"},"15387":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-171","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"`macOS 15.7.4`","locale":"en"},"15388":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-172","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"`X-OS-Version`","locale":"en"},"15389":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-173","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"`device_brand`","locale":"en"},"15390":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-174","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"`Apple`","locale":"en"},"15391":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-175","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#trae-trae","content":"`X-Device-Brand`","locale":"en"},"15392":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-176","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#qoder-qoder-qodercn","content":"Alibaba Qoder's international edition (`qoder`, `openapi.qoder.sh`) and China edition (`qodercn`, `openapi.qoder.com.cn`) are two channels; accounts and models do not carry over between them.","locale":"en"},"15393":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-177","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#qoder-qoder-qodercn","content":"**Sign-in**: `hoshimi login qoder` or `hoshimi login qodercn` opens the device authorization page on `qoder.com` / `qoder.cn`, and the gateway polls for the result; no local callback is needed. The sign-in generates a `machine_id` that renewal requests carry, so keep it in the account.","locale":"en"},"15394":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-178","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#qoder-qoder-qodercn","content":"**Models**: the two editions have different tables: 17 international IDs (`auto`, `ultimate`, `performance`, `efficient`, `smodel`, `cmodel`, `qmodel_38max`, …) and 14 China IDs (including the China-only `q37fmodel` and `gm51model`). Sending one edition's exclusive ID to the other always fails.","locale":"en"},"15395":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-179","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#qoder-qoder-qodercn","content":"**Check-in**: claiming the campaign reward needs the machine token cached by the Qoder desktop client. The adapter looks for `Qoder` (or `Qoder CN`) `/SharedClientCache/cache/machine_token.json` under `%APPDATA%`, `~/Library/Application Support` or `~/.config`; on a machine without Qoder desktop installed, check-in fails. The station refreshes its campaigns at 10:00 UTC+8.","locale":"en"},"15396":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-180","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#qoder-qoder-qodercn","content":"**Note**: the official client uses an encrypted WASM inference path; Hoshimi uses the public OpenAI-compatible endpoint, which may answer `503`. Matching headers, models and renewal do not mean inference behaves exactly as in the official client.","locale":"en"},"15397":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-181","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#qoder-qoder-qodercn","content":"**Account fields**: `access_token`, `security_oauth_token`, `refresh_token`, `machine_id`.","locale":"en"},"15398":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-182","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#qoder-cli-qodercli-qodercli-cn","content":"The same two editions, reached the way the official Qoder CLI reaches them: the signed `agent_chat_generation` endpoint instead of the public OpenAI-compatible one. Ported from the `pi-provider-qoder` extension, including its client impersonation. The lanes are separate from `qoder` / `qodercn` — different credentials, different catalogues — and both can be configured at once.","locale":"en"},"15399":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-183","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#qoder-cli-qodercli-qodercli-cn","content":"**Sign-in**: `hoshimi login qodercli --manual` (or `qodercli-cn`) opens the account's integrations page and asks for a Personal Access Token. Create one at https\\://qoder.com/account/integrations (international) or https\\://qoder.com.cn/account/integrations (China). In the web UI, **Sign in** shows the same paste field, and **Add account → Personal Access Token** files the token directly. A token exported as `QODER_API_KEY` / `QODER_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN` / `QODER_PAT` (or the `QODERCN_*` equivalents) signs the lane in without a prompt.","locale":"en"},"15400":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-184","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#qoder-cli-qodercli-qodercli-cn","content":"**Browser login (international only)**: `hoshimi login qodercli` without `--manual` opens Qoder's device authorization page and polls for the approval, while the same session still accepts a pasted PAT — whichever answers first wins. The China edition has no device flow. A browser credential carries no PAT, so it renews against `{center}/algo/api/v3/user/refresh_token` instead of re-exchanging.","locale":"en"},"15401":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-185","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#qoder-cli-qodercli-qodercli-cn","content":"**Token exchange**: a `pt-…` token is not an API credential. The adapter exchanges it at `{openApi}/api/v1/jobToken/exchange` for a job token (`jt-…`, one day) plus a job refresh token, reads the account identity from `/api/v1/userinfo`, and re-exchanges on renewal. The PAT stays in the account so renewal can repeat the exchange; a PAT the station refuses takes the account out of rotation until a human signs in again.","locale":"en"},"15402":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-186","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#qoder-cli-qodercli-qodercli-cn","content":"**Request signing**: every catalogue and chat request carries `Authorization: Bearer COSY.<payload>.<sig>`. The payload encrypts the identity (AES-128-CBC, key reused as IV) under an RSA-encrypted key, and the signature is an MD5 over payload, key, timestamp, the exact encoded body and the signed path. The header set declares a CLI client (`Cosy-Clienttype: 5`, machine id/type/OS, `Cosy-Data-Policy: disagree`, `Login-Version: v2`). The client version follows the latest Qoder CLI release (checked once a day, cached in the data directory), because the gateway serves a reduced catalogue to clients that lag behind.","locale":"en"},"15403":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-187","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#qoder-cli-qodercli-qodercli-cn","content":"**Body encoding**: chat bodies use Qoder's custom Base64 (`Encode=1`) — substituted alphabet, `$` padding, and the three blocks rotated. `region/endpoints` answers in the same encoding.","locale":"en"},"15404":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-188","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#qoder-cli-qodercli-qodercli-cn","content":"**Nodes**: chat is routed to the account's `dataNodeMap.remote_agent` node, which is what the CLI uses; the catalogue stays on the inference node. The resolved node is cached for an hour. A `403 code 110 \"Billing daily count exceeded\"` is counted per node, so the adapter rotates through the remaining candidates and remembers whichever node served the request.","locale":"en"},"15405":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-189","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#qoder-cli-qodercli-qodercli-cn","content":"**Models**: discovered live from `algo/api/v2/model/list`. The public ID is the catalogue's `display_name` without whitespace (`Auto`, `Qwen3.8-Max`, `DeepSeek-V4-Pro`, …); the upstream key (`auto`, `qmodel_38max`, `dmodel`) travels only inside the request. Context is the largest advertised option (often 1M), output is 131072, and each model's own thinking menu comes from its `thinking_config`. Static fallbacks differ per edition.","locale":"en"},"15406":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-190","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#qoder-cli-qodercli-qodercli-cn","content":"**Thinking**: the level rides in the envelope's `parameters` (`enable_thinking`, and `reasoning_effort` for effort-based models). Off takes both signals; a model with no `disabled` branch is sent the switch alone, because it rejects `reasoning_effort: \"none\"`. Leaked `<thinking>` tags and DSML tool-call markup are stripped, and a turn that produced nothing but markup is reported as a retryable error instead of a finished task.","locale":"en"},"15407":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-191","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#qoder-cli-qodercli-qodercli-cn","content":"**Busy models**: `10605` with `serviceAvailable` is the scheduler's answer. A ready request is re-sent after the hinted delay (bounded, with a fresh `request_id`); a genuinely queued one is returned as a rate limit carrying the wait, so the caller can schedule it.","locale":"en"},"15408":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-192","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#qoder-cli-qodercli-qodercli-cn","content":"**Credits**: request-level `usage.credits`, `original_credits` and `billable` are preserved, and `charged_credits` is zero for a non-billable call. **Balance** reads the account-wide period quota (personal, add-on and organization buckets); there is no daily check-in on this path.","locale":"en"},"15409":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-193","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#qoder-cli-qodercli-qodercli-cn","content":"**Account fields**: `personal_token`, `access_token`, `security_oauth_token`, `refresh_token`, `uid` / `user_id`, `nickname`, `email`, `machine_id`, `expires_at`.","locale":"en"},"15410":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-194","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#codebuddy--workbuddy-buddy-workbuddy","content":"Tencent CodeBuddy (`buddy`, `copilot.tencent.com`) and WorkBuddy international (`workbuddy`, `www.workbuddy.ai`) share one protocol on two hosts.","locale":"en"},"15411":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-195","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#codebuddy--workbuddy-buddy-workbuddy","content":"**Sign-in**: `hoshimi login buddy` or `hoshimi login workbuddy` opens an external login page, and the gateway polls for the result; no local callback is needed.","locale":"en"},"15412":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-196","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#codebuddy--workbuddy-buddy-workbuddy","content":"**Models**: CodeBuddy has 16 fallback IDs (hy4/hy3, deepseek-v4, glm-5.x, kimi, minimax-m3); WorkBuddy has 23 (including aliases such as `default-model`, gpt-5.x, gemini-3.5-flash, glm and kimi). WorkBuddy switches its User-Agent by model family.","locale":"en"},"15413":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-197","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#codebuddy--workbuddy-buddy-workbuddy","content":"**Check-in**: only CodeBuddy has a daily check-in; the WorkBuddy international station has no check-in endpoint, though its balance still works.","locale":"en"},"15414":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-198","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#codebuddy--workbuddy-buddy-workbuddy","content":"**Account fields**: `access_token`, `refresh_token`; the sign-in also saves `user_id`, `enterprise_id` and others, which the balance query uses.","locale":"en"},"15415":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-199","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#codearts-codearts","content":"Huawei Cloud CodeArts' ModelArts lane (`snap-access.cn-north-4.myhuaweicloud.com`); requests are signed with Huawei Cloud's SDK-HMAC-SHA256 scheme.","locale":"en"},"15416":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-200","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#codearts-codearts","content":"**Sign-in**: `hoshimi login codearts` opens the Huawei Cloud portal's authorization page, which calls back to a random local port of 10000 or above (the portal refuses lower ports); the token exchange carries a DPoP proof. It waits at most 5 minutes for the callback and accepts a pasted one.","locale":"en"},"15417":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-201","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#codearts-codearts","content":"**Credentials**: the result is a temporary AK/SK pair and security token with an expiry. The adapter does not renew them; sign in again when they expire.","locale":"en"},"15418":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-202","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#codearts-codearts","content":"**Models**: discovered from the station's built-in model list (`-VL` models excluded), with `GLM-5.x`, `deepseek-v4*`, `openpangu-2.0-*` and others as the fallback.","locale":"en"},"15419":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-203","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#codearts-codearts","content":"**Benefit models**: requests for models in `options.benefit_models` (default `glm-5.3-flash` and `deepseek-v4.1-flash`) carry a `maas_type: benefit` header; if the station rejects the header, the request is retried without it.","locale":"en"},"15420":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-204","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#codearts-codearts","content":"**Check-in**: claims the \"daily login\" campaign; token-billed and non-credit-billed accounts are outside the campaign.","locale":"en"},"15421":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-205","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#loomy-loomy","content":"iFlytek Loomy (`loomyad.xunfei.cn`), OpenAI-compatible.","locale":"en"},"15422":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-206","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#loomy-loomy","content":"**Sign-in**: `hoshimi login loomy` starts a local page showing a WeChat QR code; scan and confirm. A WeChat account using Loomy for the first time must bind a phone number on the same page (request and enter the SMS code). The page is served only on `127.0.0.1`, so open it in a browser on the same machine.","locale":"en"},"15423":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-207","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#loomy-loomy","content":"**Credentials**: the session lasts about 14 days and the adapter does not renew it; sign in again when it expires.","locale":"en"},"15424":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-208","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#loomy-loomy","content":"**Requests**: the token is sent both as `Authorization: Bearer` and as a `token` header (the chat and control endpoints each accept one of them).","locale":"en"},"15425":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-209","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#loomy-loomy","content":"**Account fields**: `access_token`, `userid`, `expires_at`.","locale":"en"},"15426":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-210","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#raccoon-raccoon","content":"SenseTime Raccoon (`xiaohuanxiong.com`), OpenAI-compatible.","locale":"en"},"15427":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-211","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#raccoon-raccoon","content":"**Sign-in**: `hoshimi login raccoon` opens the station's WeChat QR page, and the gateway polls for the result; no local callback is needed.","locale":"en"},"15428":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-212","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#raccoon-raccoon","content":"**Models**: a fixed list such as `sn-sensenova-6-8-flash`, `sn-glm-5-3`, `sn-kimi-k3` and `sn-deepseek-v4-1-flash`.","locale":"en"},"15429":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-213","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#raccoon-raccoon","content":"**Account fields**: `access_token`, `refresh_token`, `device_id`, `office_identity` (the organisation code, sent as `X-Org-Code`).","locale":"en"},"15430":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-214","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#lobsterai-lobsterai","content":"Youdao LobsterAI (`lobsterai-server.youdao.com`), OpenAI-compatible. The model catalogue is read live from the station, with 19 built-in IDs as the fallback.","locale":"en"},"15431":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-215","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#lobsterai-lobsterai","content":"**Sign-in**: `hoshimi login lobsterai` opens the `lobsterai.youdao.com` portal, which calls back to a temporary local port; a pasted callback is accepted.","locale":"en"},"15432":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-216","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#lobsterai-lobsterai","content":"**Note**: the `uuid` and `firstKeyfrom` generated at sign-in are sent with every renewal request; do not remove them from the account or renewal fails.","locale":"en"},"15433":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-217","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#lobsterai-lobsterai","content":"**Account fields**: `access_token`, `refresh_token`, `uuid`.","locale":"en"},"15434":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-218","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#codex-codex","content":"The Codex lane signed in with a ChatGPT account (`chatgpt.com/backend-api/codex`), using the OpenAI Responses protocol; its allowance comes from the ChatGPT subscription.","locale":"en"},"15435":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-219","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#codex-codex","content":"**Sign-in**: `hoshimi login codex` opens OpenAI's consent page and calls back to the fixed local address `localhost:1455` (the redirect registered for the Codex client), so that port must be free; only one Codex sign-in can run at a time. A pasted callback is accepted.","locale":"en"},"15436":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-220","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#codex-codex","content":"**Requests**: system and developer messages are merged into `instructions`, and `max_output_tokens`, `temperature` and `top_p` are not sent; the account's `account_id` is sent as the `ChatGPT-Account-Id` header.","locale":"en"},"15437":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-221","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#codex-codex","content":"**Models**: read from the account's model catalogue, or declared with `models` on the account.","locale":"en"},"15438":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-222","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#eac-eac","content":"EAC is a co-paid relay. It has no anonymous mode: it is enabled only when an account is configured, and **Channels** marks it as needing authorization. On a fresh install, run `hoshimi login eac` (or click **Sign in** in **Channels**) to authorise the bundled relay with GitHub; on success it creates the `eac-default` account with `relay: \"bundled\"`. You can also add a custom worker relay or a direct Bearer relay. Its models include `deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4.1-flash`, `moonshotai/kimi-*`, `z-ai/glm-5.3*` and `openai/gpt-oss-20b`, plus the relayed `opencode/deepseek-v4.1-flash-free` and `opencode/glm-5.3-flash-free`. Relay modes, signing and the authorization file are covered in EAC.","locale":"en"},"15439":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-223","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#zhipu-zhipu","content":"Zhipu's BigModel open platform (`open.bigmodel.cn/api/paas/v4`). It is a fixed station reached with a key, not an aggregator.","locale":"en"},"15440":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-224","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#zhipu-zhipu","content":"**Adding an account**: create an API key in the bigmodel.cn console, then **Add account** under **Channels** › **Zhipu GLM (BigModel)**, or write it into `config.json`.","locale":"en"},"15441":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-225","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#zhipu-zhipu","content":"**Models**: the live listing comes first (other models the account's balance covers appear too). When it cannot be reached, the 7 free IDs are the fallback: `glm-4.7-flash`, `glm-4.5-flash`, `glm-4-flash-250414`, `glm-z1-flash`, `glm-4.6v-flash`, `glm-4.1v-thinking-flash`, `glm-4v-flash`.","locale":"en"},"15442":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-226","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#zhipu-zhipu","content":"**International station**: set `options.base_url` to `https://api.z.ai/api/paas/v4` to move the whole channel to api.z.ai.","locale":"en"},"15443":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-227","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#zhipu-zhipu","content":"**Thinking**: text models without a menu leave the caller's request untouched; thinking-by-construction models such as Z1 and V-Thinking use the budget ladder.","locale":"en"},"15444":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-228","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#renewal-check-in-and-balances","content":"Two timers are switched in **Settings**: **Credential renewal** (`server.auto_refresh`) and **Daily check-in** (`server.auto_checkin`), both on by default.","locale":"en"},"15445":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-229","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#renewal-check-in-and-balances","content":"**Renewal**: starts 30 seconds after the gateway boots and checks every 30 minutes, renewing accounts that expire within the hour or record no expiry (only accounts with a `refresh_token`). When a station refuses the refresh token, the account is marked **Needs login** and taken out of rotation until you sign in again. A renewed token is written back to its own account only. To renew by hand, use **Renew now** in the channel detail (the whole channel, or one account from its menu) or **Renew every account** at the top of **Channels**; the API is `GET /api/v1/refresh` (status) and `POST /api/v1/refresh` (renew now).","locale":"en"},"15446":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-230","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#renewal-check-in-and-balances","content":"**Check-in**: starts 30 seconds after boot and claims once a day per account, by the UTC+8 calendar day, one account after another (stations rate-limit parallel requests). A station answering \"already claimed today\" counts as done. To check in by hand, use **Check in all** at the top of **Channels**, or **Claim now** in a channel's menu; **Recent check-ins** shows the channel's latest results.","locale":"en"},"15447":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-231","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#renewal-check-in-and-balances","content":"**Balance**: supporting stations can report a balance or quota. Separately, the gateway reads the remaining allowance passively from the rate-limit headers of every station response and shows it in the channel's **Allowance** section, with no extra requests.","locale":"en"},"15448":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-232","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#renewal-check-in-and-balances","content":"Capability","locale":"en"},"15449":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-233","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#renewal-check-in-and-balances","content":"Channels","locale":"en"},"15450":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-234","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#renewal-check-in-and-balances","content":"Renewal","locale":"en"},"15451":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-235","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#renewal-check-in-and-balances","content":"`cline`, `gemini`, `minimax`, `trae`, `qoder`, `qodercn`, `qodercli`, `qodercli-cn`, `buddy`, `workbuddy`, `raccoon`, `lobsterai`, `codex`","locale":"en"},"15452":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-236","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#renewal-check-in-and-balances","content":"Daily check-in","locale":"en"},"15453":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-237","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#renewal-check-in-and-balances","content":"`minimax`, `trae`, `qoder`, `qodercn`, `buddy`, `codearts`, `loomy`, `lobsterai`","locale":"en"},"15454":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-238","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#renewal-check-in-and-balances","content":"Balance","locale":"en"},"15455":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-239","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#renewal-check-in-and-balances","content":"`cline`, `gemini` (quota windows), `minimax`, `trae`, `qoder`, `qodercn`, `qodercli`, `qodercli-cn`, `buddy`, `workbuddy`, `codearts`, `loomy`, `raccoon`, `lobsterai`","locale":"en"},"15456":{"id":"/en/docs/providers-stations-240","page_id":"/en/docs/providers-stations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/providers-stations#renewal-check-in-and-balances","content":"The related routes are in the management API; the UI