s `running` says one runs, and `waiting` that it waits for an approval; the list says so too, for every conversation."],[9186,"A reply (or a compaction) is working in it now, whether or not anything follows it"],[12250,"A reply calls tools for as many rounds as it takes: there is no limit, and it ends when the model answers without calling one. **Stop** (or Esc) ends the reply at once. A running `shell` command is stopped with everything it started; a call waiting for approval or being reviewed is dropped; calls not yet run are marked **Stopped**. What the reply said and did so far is kept. Background commands keep running: stop them above the composer."],[12597,"A reply runs on the server, not in the page. Opening another chat, starting a new one, leaving the Playground or reloading the page does not stop it: it goes on in the background, and several chats can work at the same time. Open the chat again to watch it from where it is, with what it wrote so far; it can be stopped from there too. A reply that ends while no page shows it is kept, and its chat is named as usual."],[9368,"A reply that called a tool or was steered keeps its `steps`, in order. Every step has a `type` and a `round` (from 0, one per round of tool calls):"],[9360,"A reply that completes while nothing follows it names a conversation still without a title, as `POST .../title` would."],[9263,"A reply that used tools (or was steered, or compacted), step by step; empty otherwise"],[9352,"A reply with one tool call looks like this (messages shortened):"],[9266,"A reply's tokens as the station counted them: `last` (its last round) and `total` (all rounds), each with `input`, `cached`, `output`, `reasoning`; `rounds` counted; `context`, what the window held as it ended, and its `source` (`usage`, or `estimate` for a station that reports none). Empty when unknown"],[8334,"A report for a range"],[13394,"A request for an ID tries the accounts that declare it in `models` first, then accounts with no `model