hy it needs approval, as for `waiting`. Then `running`, `denied`, or `waiting` when the review came to no decision"],[8146,"Besides chat models, a station's `/models` list often carries image and video generators, embeddings, rerankers, transcription and other endpoints. `agg` decides, row by row and station by station, which rows are chat models:"],[12492,"Besides probes, the gateway remembers model failures while serving: a station answering 404/410 for a model (or 400/422 with a body that says the model was removed) counts once, and three within 10 minutes ban the model for the rest of this run. A banned model shows as **Unavailable** (over any probe verdict), and requests for it get `503 model_unavailable` at once, without upstream traffic. A restart, or `POST /api/v1/models/unavailable/reset`, lifts every ban:"],[12114,"Binary files (with a NUL byte near the start) are refused."],[8566,"Block"],[8829,"Body `{\"provider\": \"<provider>\"}`; omitted means every provider"],[10845,"Body limit is not positive"],[9170,"boolean"],[9173,"boolean"],[9185,"boolean"],[9188,"boolean"],[10672,"boolean"],[10696,"boolean"],[10700,"boolean"],[10704,"boolean"],[10742,"boolean"],[10787,"boolean"],[10805,"boolean"],[11739,"Both"],[13554,"Both accept `base_url` in place of the built address. Set `protocol` or `model_protocols` (see the end of this page) only for a protocol the upstream really supports."],[8506,"Both endpoints check the outer shape of the request first and answer `400` (in Anthropic's shape) when it fails:"],[10605,"Both keys, the channel accounts' tokens and proxy URLs are stored in plain text in `config.json` in the data directory. The file is replaced atomically on each write and restricted to its owner where the file system allows. `hoshimi config show` and `hoshimi config get` print them as `***`; the Web UI and the settings API never return their values. Error messages saved in the usage statistics have anything shaped like a key replaced with `***`. See Data