g a name with a control, the text element has `min-width: 0` (the test lists the components and selectors)"],[11364,"in a temporary data folder it builds the app and, through `TestClient`, requests `/health`, the home page (which must contain \"Hoshimi\"), every file under `assets/` and `/api/v1/providers`, and checks there is a favicon."],[14884,"In Chat requests, `max_completion_tokens` becomes `max_tokens` (`minimax-chat` and `wandb` use `max_completion_tokens` instead); services that do not accept the `developer` role get `system`."],[11419,"In the `pypi` environment, downloads the `distributions` artifact and runs `twine upload dist/* --skip-existing --non-interactive`"],[9171,"In the archive"],[7885,"In the data directory: `~/.local/share/hoshimi` on Linux, `~/Library/Application Support/hoshimi` on macOS, `%APPDATA%\\hoshimi` on Windows; `HOSHIMI_DATA_DIR` moves it elsewhere. `config.json` holds the settings and accounts; `hoshimi.db` holds usage, check-ins, probe verdicts and Playground conversations."],[10151,"In the Playground, **Copy as API request** in a reply's **More actions** menu copies the Chat Completions request behind that reply as a curl command that reads the key from `$HOSHIMI_API_KEY`, a handy starting point."],[12653,"In the reply"],[10578,"In the Web UI this is **Settings** › **Security** › **Allowed CIDRs**; press Enter after each value."],[10556,"In the Web UI, fill in the **Tool access key** and **Model API key** under **Settings** › **Access** › **Keys**; they apply as soon as they are saved. Keys are stored in the config file and never shown again: the page only says **A tool access key is set.**, and the settings API only returns whether each is set (`access_token_configured`, `model_api_key_configured`)."],[10299,"In the Web UI, open **Settings** › **Network**, choose **Automatic (environment proxy)**, **Direct** or **Proxy**, fill in the **Proxy URL** and save. Or write it in `config.json`:"],[7829,"In worker mode a leaked request c