s recorded on the **Usage** page, with the origin `chat`, `responses` or `classify`."],[11444,"The interface alone"],[13146,"The interface follows the system language by default: English, 简体中文 and 日本語 are available, and **Settings › General › Language** fixes one. Theme, colour, contrast and motion are in **Settings › Appearance**. These are browser preferences: they are kept in the current browser, not in the server's config file."],[11982,"The interface language follows the system (English, Simplified Chinese and Japanese are available); pin one under **Settings › General › Language**. Theme, colour, contrast and motion are under **Settings › Appearance**. These preferences are kept in this browser only, not on the server."],[15582,"The interface opens on the **Overview** page. The **Channels** section already holds two channels, **OpenCode Zen** and **Kilo AI**, both marked **No account needed**. They are the anonymous entry points that are on by default; which models they offer depends on the upstream catalogue, quota and service state at the time."],[11945,"The interface text exists in English, Simplified Chinese and Japanese, with the same keys and placeholders."],[11855,"The interface text lives in three files in `src/i18n/`: `en.ts` is the source, `zh-CN.ts` and `ja.ts` are the translations. In a component:"],[11846,"The interface's TypeScript types come from the server's OpenAPI document. After changing a management API request or response model, regenerate and commit:"],[13533,"The JSON below are fragments of `providers` in the data folder's `config.json`, not files to place next to the program. Replace the placeholders and enable only the channels you use; restart after editing the file. **Add account** under **Channels** takes effect immediately, and its form lists the fields for each **Authentication method**."],[14854,"The key, sent as `Authorization: Bearer` (an Anthropic API key is sent as `x-api-key`). `access_token` or `token` are also accepted. An