<port>`"],[8197,"The server will not start"],[11737,"The server's address"],[13247,"The service uses the data folder of the user it runs as; to choose the location, add `Environment=HOSHIMI_DATA_DIR=/srv/hoshimi` under `[Service]` (see Environment variables). `GET /health` needs no key and returns `{\"status\":\"ok\"}`, which makes it a liveness check:"],[12512,"The share of input tokens read from the upstream cache"],[12732,"The share of the window (0.5 to 0.95) at which a conversation is compacted"],[10793,"The share of the window at which a conversation is compacted; sooner when what is left could not hold a reply"],[11374,"The shared checks: Ruff, ty, pytest, the Web UI and API contract; see Testing"],[11830,"The shared component library, exported from `ui/index.ts`; also `layers.ts` and `motion/`"],[11824,"The shell and its navigation destinations; the route table"],[10781,"The shell commands run in when the model names none: `auto` is bash (`sh` without it; PowerShell on Windows, `cmd` without it). `\"pwsh\"` is accepted for `powershell`. A shell that is not installed falls back to `auto`"],[12067,"The shield menu in the composer"],[7833,"The signature covers the body's hash, so the body is serialized once and the same bytes are signed and sent; anything that re-encodes the body after signing makes the relay's check fail."],[11630,"The site can live under a sub-path: `VITE_BASE_PATH` sets Vite's `base`, and the routes and the search index follow it. Pages on the backup carry a canonical link to the Netlify site, so search engines treat the main site as the original. CI's shared checks also type-check, test and build the site."],[11551,"The site lives in the repository's `site/` folder, built with TanStack Start, Fumadocs (MDX) and Tailwind, and installed and run with bun."],[11530,"The site tasks are covered in Documentation site. Run `python scripts/dev.py check` once before committing: it covers CI's Python and Web UI checks."],[11826,"The six pages: Overview, Models, Channels, Usage, Playground, Settings"],[12057,"The six tools"],[11742,"The six widths from 320 to 1600"],[12996,"The span of the same length just before"],[10925,"The standard library, httpx, pydantic, cryptography and the optional cloud SDKs"],[10385,"The station does not serve the region of this egress"],[8305,"The station does not serve this egress's region. Use a proxy route in another region"],[8307,"The station grants its free tier to its own clients only"],[10382,"The station only grants its free tier to its own clients"],[12702,"The station refused the image; the reply was retried with descriptions"],[9284,"The station refused the image; the reply was tried again with descriptions"],[12364,"The station refused the refresh token; sign in again"],[8309,"The station refused the request signature"],[10388,"The station refused the request signature"],[12484,"The station refused this model specifically"],[12482,"The station refuses to serve this network egress"],[9780,"The station to sign into; omit it to list the stations that offer an interactive login"],[13279,"The station's OpenAI root. When both are given, `base_url` wins over `preset`."],[12383,"The status above the list reflects the daily timer only: **Done · time** when today's timed check-in got through, **Not yet today** otherwise."],[12738,"The system prompt is empty by default, so a model gets only the conversation and the tool descriptions. The prompt below gives it the rest: when to act and when to ask, how to use the tools well, how to take approvals, steering and compaction, and how its reply is rendered here. Paste it into **Settings › General › Playground › System prompt**. It suits chats with and without tools, and any model; replies follow the language the user writes in."],[9746,"The table has **Model** and **Provider** columns. A model id offered by several channels is listed once, under the channel that comes first."],[9752,"The table's columns are **Id**, **Name**, **Accounts** and **Models**; switched-off channels are listed under it as `disabled: …`. The account count leaves out the built-in anonymous identity of the anonymous channels."],[9760,"The table's columns are **Id**, **Name**, **Base URL** and **Key env**, followed by a usage hint:"],[11426,"The tag runs CI once more: it checks the tag against the version, skips the files PyPI already has, then creates a GitHub release with the distributions and generated notes."],[11452,"The task runner; see below"],[13511,"The terminal prints a verification link and a code (in the Web UI, click **Sign in**; the dialog shows the **Verification code**). Confirm in the browser and the account is written to `config.json`. Kilo returns a long-lived key, not a renewable OAuth token, so it is never renewed on a timer."],[8207,"The terminal running `hoshimi serve`"],[11840,"The test environment: `setup.ts` (gives happy-dom an `ElementInternals`), `motion-zero.css` (every motion duration at zero)"],[11274,"The test layout and shared fixtures are in Testing."],[9303,"The text. A message needs text or an attachment (`400` otherwise)"],[9239,"The text. For a reply that used tools, its text steps joined by blank lines"],[13409,"The thinking-level menu, in display order. Including `disabled` makes thinking switchable off."],[10728,"The three keys also accept the singular spellings `allow_cidr`, `allow_host` and `allow_origin`, and a single comma-separated string instead of a list. A save writes them back as plural lists. The checks are described in Access control."],[13060,"The time for today's calls, the date for older ones; hover for the full time"],[7909,"The timer starts only when the server starts, and turning the switch off while it runs does not stop it. Also, `hoshimi serve` overrides the setting at start with `--refresh/--no-refresh` (on by default), and `--checkin/--no-checkin` likewise. To turn them off, start with `hoshimi serve --no-refresh` or `--no-checkin`."],[8286,"The timers start only when the server starts. `hoshimi serve` turns both on by default and overrides `server.auto_refresh` and `server.auto_checkin` from the configuration; to turn them off, start with `--no-refresh` or `--no-checkin`."],[12366,"The token has expired"],[15557,"The tokens of many sign-in stations expire. With **Credential renewal** on (`server.auto_refresh`, on by default) the gateway checks every 30 minutes and renews accounts that expire within the hour or record no expiry. With **Daily check-in** on (`server.auto_checkin`, on by default) it claims each supporting station's free credits once a day, by the calendar day in UTC+8. Which stations support renewal, check-in and balance queries is listed in Free stations."],[10589,"The tool access key is for you, to manage the gateway; the model API key is for the other clients on your LAN (editor plugins, agents)."],[11990,"The tool access key protects the Web UI and the management API (`/api/v1/*`, `/docs`, `/openapi.json`); the model API `/v1/*` is protected by a separate, independent **Model API key**. The Playground goes through the management API, so it needs only the tool access key. The two keys and LAN access are covered in Security."],[12737,"The tool settings (`playground.tools`, `workspace`, `approval`, `search_url`) are in Playground tools."],[10168,"The top-level `model` is the default model as `provider/model`, where the provider is `hoshimi`."],[13473,"The transport shares admission control, proxy routing and httpcore pooling. It supports HTTP/HTTPS and SOCKS5/SOCKS5H proxies, incremental streaming, connection and read/write timeouts, and releases connections when streams close early. TLS verifies certificate chains and hostnames, using HTTPX's default CA roots or `SSL_CERT_FILE` / `SSL_CERT_DIR`. Process-wide SSL settings remain unchanged."],[11967,"The two default anonymous channels"],[13431,"The two free lanes that are on by default and need no account, OpenCode Zen and Kilo: what they offer, how to turn them off, how a key widens the catalogue, and how their protocols are handled."],[10520,"The two keys"],[10551,"The two keys are independent: the tool access key does not open `/v1/*`, and the model API key does not open `/api/*`."],[7806,"The two relay modes"],[11898,"The unit tests read the source; sideways overflow in real browsers is checked by `scripts/check_layout.py`, see Testing."],[10373,"The upstream answered with a Cloudflare challenge (`cf-mitigated: challenge`)"],[8299,"The upstream answered with a Cloudflare challenge. Hoshimi does not solve challenges; try another route or later"],[9592,"The upstream failed"],[8981,"The upstream failed; `response.error` says why"],[8795,"The upstream protocol: `chat`, `responses`, `messages` and so on"],[9600,"The upstream refused the account's credentials"],[8270,"The upstream rejected this account's refresh token (log: `<channel>/<account>: refresh token rejected, account needs a new login`). The account leaves rotation and renewal skips it until you sign in again:"],[8394,"The upstream reported no token usage"],[10104,"The upstream returned an error after the stream began, Hoshimi ended the stream with an error event, and Codex gave up after reconnecting a few times. Open the **Usage** page to read the call's error. In local tests the same tool-calling task finished on some models while others were refused by the upstream with `HTTP 400` on the second turn; another model usually works"],[9606,"The upstream's `404` / `410`"],[8988,"The upstream's model name; a name several providers share is listed once (the first provider in order)"],[9598,"The upstream's status"],[9602,"The upstream's status"],[9594,"The upstream's status (usually `429`)"],[12968,"The Usage page: choose a range or a single day, read the headline tiles and the token and speed charts, break usage down by model, provider, account and API, and look at each call."],[9397,"The user or the review model denied it; it did not run. Denied by the review model, `output` is what the model was told; denied by the user, it is empty"],[13602,"The values are `chat`, `responses` and `messages`, with the aliases `openai-completions`, `openai-responses` and `anthropic-messages` also accepted. `google` and `google-vertex` use `gemini` or `chat`. Set these only for protocols the upstream really supports. More protocol-related options are in Local and compatible endpoints."],[12458,"The verdict of the last probe, below; **Not probed** for a model no round has reached"],[8677,"The version"],[8750,"The version"],[11320,"The version"],[11802,"The Vite dev server (port 5173)"],[11928,"The Vue 3 + Vite interface; `dist/` ships in the package"],[11904,"The way in for contributors: what Hoshimi is made of, what is authoritative, the conventions that apply everywhere, and what each development page covers."],[11468,"The Web UI (`hoshimi/webui/`) and the documentation site (`site/`) both use bun to install, build and test; CI uses bun 1.4.2. When `bun` is not on `PATH`, `dev.py` prints one line saying so and exits with status 127 rather than a traceback."],[8230,"The Web UI build files are missing and only the API is served. Packages installed from PyPI include the build; when running from source, build the Web UI first; see Development setup."],[11012,"The Web UI derives its root from the URL of its own script, so it needs no change under a prefix."],[11782,"The Web UI lives in `hoshimi/webui/`: a Vue 3 + Vite + TypeScript app following the Material Design 3 system it shares with its sister project Mizuoto. It talks to the server over HTTP only; the built `dist/` ships in the Python package and the server serves it as static files. This page covers its structure, its contract with the server, and the rules a change to the interface must keep, most of them enforced by tests under `src/`."],[11441,"The Web UI: bun"],[7961,"The Web UI's **Models** page and the Playground load the catalogue through `GET /api/v1/catalog/stream` (SSE): cached results come first, then each channel's fresh result as it arrives. At most 8 fetches run at once; a round waits at most 20 seconds, marks unfinished channels as timed out and keeps the models already received. The standard `/v1/models` stays plain JSON."],[7886,"The Web UI's **Settings** › **About** also shows the **Data directory**, **Config file** and **Database**."],[10451,"the Web UI's **Settings** › **About** shows the **Data directory**, **Config file** and **Database**;"],[10635,"The Web UI's **Settings** and **Channels** pages, or `PATCH /api/v1/settings`"],[9071,"The Web UI's Playground does everything through these routes, so a script can do the same: keep conversations, stream replies, run the tools and answer their approvals. Everything a model is sent (the system prompt, file text, image descriptions, earlier tool calls) is put together on the server; a client only says what to add and where."],[11947,"The Web UI's TypeScript types are generated from the server's OpenAPI document (`src/api/schema.d.ts`) and committed; CI regenerates them and fails on a difference. A change to a management API model means running `python scripts/dev.py typegen` and committing the result."],[13072,"The whole call"],[10900,"The whole configuration is validated before writing, so set keys that depend on each other in one go. To switch to proxy mode, for example, set the whole `network` object; `network.mode proxy` on its own is refused for lack of a proxy URL."],[12595,"The whole conversation scrolls as one. A tool's output, a compaction summary and a question being edited scroll on their own when they are long; once one reaches its top or its end, scrolling on in the same direction (the wheel, a trackpad or a swipe) moves the conversation instead of stopping there."],[8898,"The whole conversation; Hoshimi keeps no history"],[9480,"The whole of Hoshimi's HTTP interface: where the model, management and Playground APIs live and which key each uses, request checks and error shapes,