tead; see the sections below."],[13485,"These IDs use the thinking menus declared by the reference implementation; other IDs follow the shared capability table (see Model behaviour)."],[15457,"These key-billed services also support `hoshimi login`; see their pages for details:"],[9709,"These options apply to this start only and are not written to `config.json`. An empty string for `--access-token`, `--model-api-key` or `--default-model` has no effect; the configured value is kept."],[12941,"These options are kept in the current browser and affect only it:"],[8517,"These provider options (in `providers.<id>.options`) adjust the behaviour:"],[11950,"These repositories sit as local clones in the repository root, to compare protocols and behaviour against. They are all in `.gitignore`: they never enter this repository and Hoshimi does not depend on them."],[14824,"These services' addresses, protocols and catalogue endpoints are built in, so an account needs only a key."],[15213,"These translations make requests acceptable to NIM; they are not full OpenAI feature parity. Whether a request succeeds is finally decided by the key's permissions, quota and model access."],[8498,"These two endpoints are compatible with Anthropic Messages and serve clients such as the Anthropic SDKs and Claude Code. The base address is `http://127.0.0.1:10600` (clients add `/v1/messages` themselves), authenticated with the model API key sent as `x-api-key` or `Authorization: Bearer` (see API overview). Usage examples are in Anthropic SDK."],[9897,"These variables must be in the environment of the process that runs Hoshimi, which matters especially for a system service. The account formats are in Cloud platforms."],[9985,"Thinking and effort"],[7974,"Thinking can be switched off"],[13489,"Thinking can be switched off"],[8001,"Thinking is limited through the output ceiling: `light` 2,048, `balanced` 8,192, `deep` the model's full output limit"],[13558,"Thinking is set with `reasoning_effort`, or 