r streaming, reasoning effort and tool calls."],[12691,"What you see"],[11963,"What you see after starting Hoshimi for the first time: what appears in the data folder, the layout of the interface, signing in when an access key is set, the two anonymous channels that are on by default, and where everything is."],[12007,"What you see the first time"],[3560,"wheel 和 sdist 的输出目录"],[7914,"When"],[8965,"When"],[9317,"When"],[11412,"When"],[14818,"When `api_key` (or `access_token`, `token`) has a value it is sent as `Authorization: Bearer`; otherwise no auth header is sent."],[9978,"When `config.json` cannot be parsed, every command that reads the configuration (including `serve`) refuses to run, and first copies the file to `config.json.corrupt-<timestamp>`; the error message gives the copy's path. Fix or delete `config.json` and try again. The file's location and format are in Configuration."],[10876,"When `config.json` is not valid JSON (or not a JSON object), the server refuses to start. It first copies the file to `config.json.corrupt-<UTC time>` and names that copy in the error message. Fix or remove `config.json`, then start again."],[13257,"When `HOSHIMI_DATA_DIR` is set, the data folder is wherever it points. `hoshimi config path` prints the full path of the configuration file; the folder it is in is the data folder."],[9012,"When `model` is absent, `server.default_model` is used (**Settings** › **General** › **Default model**, or `hoshimi serve --default-model`)."],[8221,"When `server.host` is `0.0.0.0` or a LAN address, a tool access key and `security.allow_cidrs` are required, or the server refuses to start (exit code 4). Follow \"Opening the gateway to your LAN\" in Access control, or set `server.host` back to `127.0.0.1`."],[11342,"When a `v<version>` tag is pushed, the build job requires the tag to match `hoshimi/version.py` (`0.5.0` goes with `v0.5.0`) and fails otherwise."],[10604,"When a browser opens the Web UI through the public name, writes such as saving settings or sending a message carry the public `Origin`, which differs from the forwarded `Host`, and are refused (`403 bad_origin`). Add the public address (such as `https://hoshimi.example.com`) to `security.allow_origins`."],[8260,"When a catalogue fetch fails, the gateway keeps the last good catalogue and retries after 30 seconds; the **Models** page says **Catalogue unavailable or timed out: …. Existing models are retained.** A loading round waits at most 20 seconds and marks slow channels as timed out; refresh a little later."],[8097,"When a channel has no account left to try at all (all need a login or are held), the answer is `502`: `Provider '…' exhausted all accounts.`"],[8064,"When a channel has several accounts, a request starts with the first usable one, skipping accounts that need a login or are held out of rotation. After a failure, the kind of failure decides what happens next:"],[8289,"When a channel request fails, the message looks like `<channel>: <category>; <advice>`, with the same categories as `kind` in the network diagnostics:"],[10298,"When a configured proxy cannot be reached, the request fails. It **never** falls back to a direct connection."],[12683,"When a conversation nears the window, it is **compacted**: a model writes a summary of the conversation so far (the goal, the decisions and why, what is done and still to do, the files involved, the next step), and from then on the model reads that summary, with your latest messages kept word for word, in place of everything before it. The conversation itself stays on screen. A line marks where it was compacted; press it to read the summary."],[8318,"When a model cannot read images (`vision` is `false` in its capabilities), the Playground has the **Image model** (`playground.vision_model`) describe the image in words first, and says above the reply **The image “…” was described by …, because this model can’t read images.** When no model can read it, or the **Image model** is **Off**, it says **The image “…” was left out: no model could read it.**"],[8321,"When a model does not support tool calls, or the upstream refuses `tools` before the reply starts (an error mentioning tool, tool_choice or function call), the Playground retries without tools and says **… can’t call tools, so it answered without them.** Pick a model that supports tools (**Tools** on the **Models** page). Turning tools on and the approval modes are covered in Playground tools."],[8281,"When a model is saturated (such as CodeBuddy's `14003`, \"model busy\"), the gateway returns the upstream's message without rotating: every account would get the same answer. Use another model or try later."],[8319,"When a model should read images but the upstream refuses the image before the reply starts (an error mentioning image, vision, multimodal and the like), the Playground retries once with descriptions and says **… refused the image, so it was sent as a description.**"],[10032,"When a model's provider has a Messages endpoint of its own (the `anthropic` provider, for example), Hoshimi forwards the request unchanged except for the model name, and the upstream handles every field Claude Code sends. Models on other providers go through protocol conversion, and recent Claude Code versions send things the conversion does not support. Tested locally with Claude Code 2.1.308 (`claude -p`), converted models answered:"],[8262,"When a new list suddenly has fewer than half the models, the old list is kept for one cycle and the log says `the catalogue came back at N of M models (likely a partial answer)`; if the next cycle agrees, it is accepted and the log says `accepting it as the station's own answer`."],[12347,"When a provider has several ways to authenticate, choose one under **Authentication method** first, such as Bedrock's **API key**, **AWS access keys**, **AWS profile**, **AWS default credentials**; Vertex's **API key**, **Google default credentials**, **Google service account file**; EAC's **Bundled EAC relay (GitHub sign-in)**, **Custom EAC worker relay**, **Direct EAC Bearer relay**."],[9617,"When a request body does not match an endpoint's schema, `/v1/messages` answers `400` (`Invalid Messages request body.`) and other endpoints answer the framework's default `422` with `{\"detail\": [...]}`."],[10218,"When a request carries both `Authorization` and `x-api-key`, `Authorization` wins."],[10225,"When a request has no `model`, Chat Completions and Responses use **Default model** from **Settings** › **General** (config key `server.default_model`, or `hoshimi serve --default-model`). Messages always requires `model`."],[7844,"When adding an EAC account on the **Channels** page you can pick the bundled relay, a custom worker relay or a direct relay. Or write it in the configuration:"],[11175,"When an account has a native Anthropic Messages endpoint, its URL and headers; `/v1/messages` then passes requests through whole"],[8606,"When both are present, `output_config.effort` wins. For models whose upstream protocol is Messages, `thinking`, `output_config` and `metadata` are passed through."],[10280,"When changes apply"],[10618,"When changes take effect"],[13124,"When channels need a hand (a new login, an expired token, an account held out of rotation, an allowance about to run out), the **Channels** icon shows how many."],[10066,"When Claude Code does not recognise a model id it prints a notice that it assumes a 200k context window; that notice comes from Claude Code itself."],[8095,"When every account has been asked and the last failure was recoverable (not credentials, quota, policy or a missing model), the gateway waits and tries the pool again, at most twice. The wait is `Retry-After` or the body's reset time when given, capped at 8 seconds; `Retry-After: 0` means at once. Otherwise it is random (a ceiling starting at 0.25 seconds that doubles, up to 8 seconds)."],[11242,"When every account has been tried and the last error is the kind that time may change, the pool makes up to `backoff_retries` more passes: it waits for the time the upstream named (at most `backoff_max_seconds`), or a random wait (full jitter) when none was named. Once content has gone out, it never retries."],[11248,"When fetching fails, the previous result is kept and fetching is retried after 30 seconds; with no earlier success, `fallback_models()` is used."],[10602,"When Hoshimi listens on loopback and a reverse proxy on the same machine forwards to it:"],[10498,"When Hoshimi runs as a system service, the service manager collects the logs (for example `journalctl`); see Installation."],[9860,"When it is not set, the data folder is:"],[9875,"When it is read"],[10633,"When it takes effect"],[10593,"When listening on a non-loopback address without the prerequisites, the server refuses to start:"],[10568,"When listening on loopback, the `Host` header is a loopback name or the listening address (DNS-rebinding protection)"],[9524,"When missing or wrong"],[7917,"When models are listed or a bare model id is looked up (including opening the **Models** page or the Playground, and `hoshimi check`), then cached for 5 minutes"],[8639,"When none is declared, or the native endpoint answers `404`, `405` or `501`, Hoshimi returns a local estimate with the header `x-hoshimi-token-count: estimate`. The estimate approximates from the UTF-8 size of `system`, `messages`, `tools` and `tool_choice` (about one token per 3 bytes, at least 1), accepts native document and tool blocks, and runs no tokenizer."],[12466,"When nothing matches, the page says **No models match**."],[8325,"When old JSON records were imported after an upgrade, this file could not be read; it was renamed aside and that record started empty. Nothing else is affected; delete it if you do not need it."],[12926,"When one channel needs a different route, **Per-channel routes** takes you to the Channels page, where the channel's **Network** section overrides it. See Network and proxies."],[15550,"When only one channel is enabled, an unknown ID is passed to it unchanged."],[10202,"When port 10600 is taken, the server moves on to the next free port; use the address it prints at start-up. **Listening address** under **Settings** › **Access** shows the port in use."],[10877,"When saved from the Web UI or the management API:"],[9846,"When set, all of Hoshimi's data moves to this folder together:"],[10137,"When streaming, read it from `chunk.choices[0].delta` with `getattr(delta, \"reasoning_content\", None)`. `reasoning_effort` takes `minimal`, `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`, `max`, or a model's own level name; the **Models** page lists each model's levels, and OpenAI-compatible API has the mapping."],[10308,"when that variable is empty, `ALL_PROXY`;"],[8284,"When the browser and Hoshimi are on different machines, the callback cannot reach Hoshimi. Use `hoshimi login <channel> --no-open --manual`: open the printed link in any browser, finish there, and paste the address the browser ended on (or the authorization code) back into the terminal. Not every station supports manual input."],[15241,"When the browser is not on the machine running Hoshimi, paste the address the browser finally lands on into **Authorization code or callback URL** and click **Submit code**."],[13483,"When the caller sets `tool_choice: \"none\"`, the field is left out of the upstream request and the gateway makes sure no tool call reaches the caller."],[12333,"When the channel needs attention, a banner under the actions lists why, such as **2 need a new login**, **1 expired**, **1 held out of rotation**, **Rate limited ×3**, **Quota header unreadable ×1**, **Only 8% of the allowance is left**."],[8263,"When the channel's network fails, the **Network** section of its **Channels** page shows errors for the **Model catalogue** operation."],[8531,"When the client disconnects, Hoshimi closes the upstream connection; a stream that has begun is not replayed on another account."],[9934,"When the configuration file is broken"],[10495,"When the database was last used by a newer Hoshimi, an older one warns at start:"],[13468,"When the first account has a key, the catalogue is no longer cut down to the free slice; the key's own permissions still apply."],[12397,"When the last reading was taken; past five minutes the subtitle says **The last reading is more than five minutes old.**"],[12444,"When the list is empty"],[8638,"When the provider declares a native counting endpoint (`anthropic` by default; others with `messages_count_tokens: true`), the body and protocol headers are forwarded and the upstream's count returned."],[7955,"When the same id appears on several channels, `/v1/models` lists only the first channel's entry. Use the `channel/model` form to pick the channel."],[13144,"When the server has a tool access key (`server.access_token`), the interface opens with **Tool access key required**. Enter the key and click **Sign in**; the interface checks it with the server first, then keeps it in this browser's localStorage and does not ask again. A wrong key shows **The tool access key is incorrect.** and does not replace a key saved earlier."],[15580,"When the server is ready, the terminal prints `SERVER_READY url=http://127.0.0.1:10600` and the browser opens that address a moment later. By default the server listens on this machine only (`127.0.0.1`), port **10600**; if that port is busy it moves to the next free one, so use the URL the terminal prints. Press Ctrl+C to stop it."],[8482,"When the server shuts down, this stream ends first so it never holds up the shutdown."],[15183,"When the service is in the table above, use its channel: it carries the service's protocol, catalogue endpoint and compatibility rules. When it is not, but speaks OpenAI Chat Completions, use agg: put the address and key in an account, and one agg channel can hold several stations."],[12341,"When the station answers, the account is written to `config.json` and joins the account pool at once, with **Signed in as** *account id*. Click **Done** to close."],[8834,"When the station needs more input (`waiting_for` is not empty), send `{\"session_id\": \"…\", \"value\": \"…\"}` to `POST /login/input`. `POST /login/cancel?session_id=<session-id>` cancels a sign-in in progress."],[12377,"When the station refuses the refresh token (401/403, or a body that says the token is invalid), the account is marked **Needs login** and is not retried: sign in again."],[10010,"When the upstream does not speak Anthropic's protocol, these settings become the model's own effort controls; the rules are in Anthropic-compatible API."],[8915,"When the upstream fails mid-stream, Hoshimi sends `data: {\"error\": {\"message\": \"…\", \"type\": \"upstream_error\"}}` and ends without `[DONE]`."],[10012,"When the upstream has a native counting endpoint (Anthropic accounts do by default), you get its count; otherwise Hoshimi returns a local estimate with the header `x-hoshimi-token-count: estimate`. The estimate approximates from the UTF-8 size of the request and runs no tokenizer. Counting generates no reply and adds no usage record."],[8591,"When the upstream protocol is not Messages, thinking settings become an effort level, which is then applied to the model by the rules in OpenAI-compatible API:"],[8103,"when the upstream rejects the refresh token itself (such as `invalid_grant`, or a `401` with no explanation), the account is marked **Needs login** and leaves rotation until you sign in again; other failures are retried next round. A bare `403` never invalidates an account."],[8914,"When the upstream reports usage, one chunk has empty `choices` and a `usage` object; `stream_options` is not needed."],[10135,"When the upstream reports usage, the stream carries one chunk with empty `choices` and a `usage` object, without `stream_options`; that is why the loop checks `chunk.choices` first."],[14882,"When the upstream speaks Anthropic Messages, `/v1/messages` requests from Anthropic clients (such as Claude Code) are passed through natively, without format conversion. Feature boundaries and client setup are in Anthropic API."],[13025,"When there are measurements, two line charts appear: **Time to first token** and **Decode speed (tok/s)**, both averages per bucket; buckets without a measurement are left as gaps rather than drawn as zero."],[14794,"When to use agg instead"],[12066,"When tools ask first"],[10773,"When tools ask first, and whom: `review` has a model judge commands, file changes and anything outside the workspace, and asks you when it cannot decide; `ask` asks you before those; `workspace` asks only before reading or changing files outside the workspace; `full` never asks. `\"auto\"`, the old name of `workspace`, is still accepted. An empty string counts as `review`"],[13145,"When you change or clear the key in **Settings › Access**, this browser switches to the new key by itself; other browsers have to sign in again. The Playground uses the management API, so it needs only the tool access key, not the model API key. For the difference between the two keys see Access and security."],[10173,"When you use models from Hoshimi's default `opencode` provider (those with `owned_by` set to `opencode` in `/v1/models`), two things concern the client:"],[8567,"Where"],[9939,"Where"],[11102,"Where"],[11976,"Where"],[15495,"Where accounts come from"],[7985,"Where capabilities come from, highest priority first:"],[12573,"Where chats are kept"],[12863,"Where commands run when the model names no shell. **Automatic** is bash (`sh` without it; PowerShell on Windows, `cmd` without it), and its help text shows the one in effect (\"Now bash\"). The menu lists only the shells installed here; a model can still ask for any other of them"],[10607,"Where config.json lives, how to change it, and every key: type, default, meaning, validation rules, and when each change takes effect."],[10533,"Where credentials are kept"],[13605,"Where each provider definition comes from, its endpoint and protocol, how it authenticates, and how far Hoshimi covers it. Generated."],[10427,"Where Hoshimi keeps its configuration, database and other files, what each holds and for how long, where the logs go, and how to back up, reset and migrate from older versions."],[9459,"Where the conversation is compacted, and the room kept for a reply"],[10428,"Where the data directory is"],[10608,"Where the file is"],[7808,"Where the GitHub authorization token comes from"],[10769,"Where the tools work; `~` is expanded. Empty means `<data directory>/workspace`"],[11319,"Where the version lives, how the wheel gets the built Web UI and is checked, what each of the four CI workflows does, how one push publishes a new version to PyPI and GitHub, and how the docs site is deployed."],[11359,"Where the wheel and sdist go"],[11969,"Where things are"],[10192,"Where to find it"],[8205,"Where to look"],[8330,"Where tokens and cache counts come from"],[12867,"Where tools start, and the only folder whose files they can edit. The help text shows the path in effect"],[11132,"Whether a default availability probe asks about this provider's models"],[13446,"Whether a model answers depends on the upstream's current models, quota and service state, and can differ by the region your network exits from. This page describes how the adapters work, not a promise about upstream availability."],[8752,"Whether a tool access key / model API key is set"],[8803,"Whether availability depends on region"],[13417,"Whether availability depends on the network exit's region."],[11261,"Whether calling it costs nothing; three-way, with `None` for \"the station did not say\""],[13403,"Whether it is a thinking model."],[11292,"Whether it is implemented; unimplemented ones are not registered"],[8378,"Whether it succeeded"],[8683,"Whether PyPI has a newer release"],[8210,"Whether the configuration reads and validates, and which channels and how many accounts would run"],[13401,"Whether the model accepts image input."],[8811,"Whether the model is held out (the station answered 404/410 on every account)"],[8376,"Whether the response was streamed"],[8805,"Whether the station says it is free; `null` when it says nothing"],[9000,"Whether thinking can be disabled"],[11265,"Whether thinking can be switched off, whether the region matters"],[8801,"Whether thinking can be turned off"],[8754,"Whether this request comes from the server's own machine"],[11002,"Whether to serve the Web UI (`hoshimi serve --no-ui` and the tests pass `False`)"],[13064,"Which account of which channel answered"],[10182,"Which API to use"],[12353,"Which fields each cloud service needs is in Cloud services and Local and compatible endpoints."],[12650,"Which model describes images is the **Image model** setting. **Automatic** takes the first model in the catalogue that reads images, skipping any the last availability probe found unavailable or region-blocked. **Off** never asks: the image is left out and the reply says so. You can also pick one model."],[10279,"Which requests are covered"],[10273,"Which route Hoshimi takes to upstream stations: environment proxies, direct or a configured proxy, per-channel overrides, which requests are covered, and how to read the network diagnostics."],[9976,"While `serve` runs, Ctrl+C shuts the server down cleanly: it ends long-lived connections such as the live usage stream first, then exits."],[12186,"While a call is reviewed, its card shows **Reviewing…** and the reply's foot line **Reviewing *tool*…**. Review time counts as the reply's own working time; time waiting for you is left out of \"Worked for\"."],[12648,"While a description is being written the reply shows \"Reading the image with *model*…\"."],[12615,"While a reply is running only `/status`, `/permissions` and `/new` run; the others say why they can't. A slash followed by something that is not a command, such as `/etc/hosts`, is sent as a message."],[12690,"While a reply runs, a line at its foot says what it is doing (writing, running or reviewing a tool, compacting the context) and for how long, second by second. The clock stops while a tool call waits for your approval; time the review model takes counts. When the reply ends, **Worked for 1m 23s** (or **Stopped after**, **Failed after**) stays beside its actions; point at it to see when it started and ended."],[12242,"While a reply with tools is running, you can add to it without stopping it. The box reads \"Add to what it’s doing…\"; type and press Enter (or the button, now **Send to the reply under way**)."],[12475,"While a round runs the button reads **Probing…**, and clicking again does not start a second one. When it ends you see **Probe round finished** and the list updates."],[9551,"While bound to a loopback address, `Host` is not `localhost`, `127.0.0.1`, `::1` or the bound address"],[13020,"While calls are running, **Running now (N)** appears under the tiles with a card per call, the same as Live activity in the top bar."],[10580,"While listening on a non-loopback address (such as `0.0.0.0`) there is no Host check; access is controlled by the network allowlist and the keys. `security.allow_hosts` (**Allowed hosts**) is saved and shown, but this version's check does not read it."],[15591,"While no model API key is set, `api_key` can be any value; once one is set, requests must send `Authorization: Bearer <model-api-key>`."],[11485,"While the API restarts, Vite's proxy prints at most one \"API is not answering\" line every 5 seconds and answers requests with HTTP 502 and `{\"code\": \"api_unreachable\", ...}`, instead of a screen full of connection errors."],[10579,"While the server listens on a loopback address (`127.x.x.x`, `localhost`, `::1`), the request's `Host` header (without its port) must be `localhost`, `127.0.0.1`, `::1` or the listening address itself; anything else gets `400 bad_host`. This stops a malicious web page from using DNS rebinding, pointing an outside domain at `127.0.0.1` to reach your gateway."],[12380,"While timed renewal is on, the Channels page refreshes every 30 seconds, so renewal results show up by themselves."],[10064,"While waiting on the upstream, a streaming response gets a `ping` event every 15 seconds, only ever between complete events."],[10003,"While waiting on the upstream, Hoshimi inserts a `ping` event between complete events every 15 seconds; the SDK skips it."],[12902,"Who may connect. Press Enter after each value, or paste several at once (separated by spaces or commas); the × on a value removes it."],[9901,"Why"],[11870,"Why"],[9248,"Why a reply failed"],[8390,"Why it ended"],[13436,"Widening the catalogue with an API key"],[2066,"Windows"],[2646,"Windows"],[2830,"Windows"],[5456,"Windows"],[9865,"Windows"],[10445,"Windows"],[10629,"Windows"],[13253,"Windows"],[10744,"Windows only: in `auto` mode, use the system proxy when no environment proxy is set"],[10277,"Windows system proxy"],[2478,"Windows 系统代理"],[2082,"Windows，没有设置 `HOSHIMI_DATA_DIR` 时"],[7908,"With **Daily check-in** on, it runs 30 seconds after the server starts and then every 24 hours, using calendar days in Beijing time (UTC+8) to decide whether today is done. Accounts are checked in one after another, never in parallel. The **Channels** page has **Claim now** and **Check in all**."],[12981,"With **Day**, a day navigator appears: the arrows step to the **Previous day** and **Next day**, and the button between them (**Today**, **Yesterday** or a date) opens a calendar. Days with usage are shaded by how many tokens they had; days after today, or before the first recorded day, cannot be chosen."],[12376,"With **Settings › Automation › Credential renewal** on (the default), the gateway starts 30 seconds after launch and goes over every account with a refresh token every 30 minutes, renewing those whose token expires within the hour or that record no expiry at all. The renewed token is written back to that account in `config.json`."],[13244,"With `--host` set to `0.0.0.0` or a LAN address, anyone who can reach this machine could spend your upstream accounts. Hoshimi refuses to start until both a tool access key (`server.access_token`) and allowed networks (`security.allow_cidrs`) are configured. The full procedure is in Security."],[9738,"With `--json`, the exit code is 0 even when no channel is enabled."],[9716,"With `--open`, the address is opened in a browser a moment later."],[9790,"With `--open`, the link opens in a browser; if no browser can be opened, you are asked to visit it by hand."],[8617,"With `\"stream\": true`, each event is sent as two lines, `event: <type>` and `data: <json>`:"],[10034,"with `CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_EXPERIMENTAL_BETAS=1`: `400 <provider>: Messages roles must be user or assistant; use top-level system.` (this version puts a `system`-role message inside `messages`)"],[10044,"With `CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_GATEWAY_MODEL_DISCOVERY=1`, Claude Code asks the gateway for its model list to fill the model picker. Hoshimi waits at most two seconds on the `GET /v1/models?limit=1000` it sends: slow providers are represented by cached, configured or built-in ids while discovery finishes in the background, and each entry carries a `display_name`."],[10325,"With `network.system_proxy` set to `true` (**Use Windows system proxy when no environment proxy exists** in the Web UI), on Windows, `auto` mode reads the system proxy settings (including their exception list) when no environment proxy was found. The option has no effect on other systems."],[8107,"With `server.auto_checkin` on, the first check-in round runs 30 seconds after start, then one every 24 hours. Days are calendar days in Beijing time (UTC+8); once an account has checked in for the day (or the station says it already has), the day is not repeated. Accounts are checked in one after another, never in parallel, to avoid tripping the stations' risk controls. Every outcome, scheduled or manual, joins a 365-day history."],[7901,"With a bare model id, the gateway takes the first channel in its built-in order that lists it, and `/v1/models` shows only that entry. To choose the channel, write `channel/model`, such as `kilo/<model id>`."],[13514,"With a credentialed account, the catalogue includes every chat model the account can see; `options.free_only: true` keeps it to free models."],[7995,"With a level, there are three cases:"],[13395,"With a single station you need no declarations. With several, use `models` to pin IDs to the right account, so a request does not land first on a station that does not know the ID."],[9642,"With a tool access key set, both addresses require it: opening them in a browser gives `401`, and the buttons are hidden. Fetch the OpenAPI document with the header:"],[12330,"With accounts: runs a renewal round for this channel"],[10582,"With an `Origin` header, it must equal the page's own origin (`http://` or `https://` plus the request's `Host`), or be listed in `security.allow_origins`, or `allow_origins` must contain `*`."],[13450,"With an account"],[11488,"With an API already running elsewhere, `python scripts/dev.py web-dev` starts only Vite. It proxies to `http://127.0.0.1:10600` by default; for an API at another address, set the `HOSHIMI_BACKEND` environment variable to it first (for example `http://127.0.0.1:10601`)."],[12246,"With an empty box, the button is still **Stop**, and Esc always stops."],[12538,"With no channel at all the section says **No providers are enabled**. Sign into a free station or add an API key on the **Channels** page; there is no file to edit and no restart."],[11992,"With no configuration at all, Hoshimi enables two channels that need no account:"],[10217,"With no model API key set, `/v1/*` checks no key. Most SDKs and tools insist on a value; any non-empty string will do."],[9892,"With no proxy variable at all, `network.system_proxy: true` falls back to the system proxy on Windows."],[9641,"With no tool access key set, the **Endpoints** section of **Overview